ce, her strained courage and scarcely upheld resolution gave way. With a cry, she sprang toward us, clasped Adrian's knees, and, saying only, \u201cO save my father!\u201d amid sobs and hysterical exclamations, released the long-barred flood of her grief.\\n\\nPoor girl!\u2014she and her father now rest side by side beneath the tall walnut-tree where her lover lies, and which she had indicated to us in her last moments. Her father, finally made aware of his daughter's peril, and unable to behold the changes in her beloved face, stubbornly retained her hand until death had made it cold and rigid. Nor afterward did he stir or utter a word, until, twelve hours later, merciful death bore him to his unbroken rest. Beneath the turf they lie, with the tree for their memorial;\u2014that sacred place remains clear to my recollection, enclosed by rugged Jura and the distant, boundless Alps; the church spire they once attended still rises among the sheltering trees; and though her hand is cold, I still fancy that the strains of holy music they cherished drift around them, comforting their mild spirits.\"}"
