 and she should be Diana to me. With every effort to cast it off, this love clings more closely\u2014this guilty love, more unnatural than hatred, which withers your hopes and destroys me forever.\\n\\nBetter to have loved despair, and safer to have kissed her.\\n\\nNo time or distance can tear from my soul what has become part of it. Since arriving here, I have not ceased for a moment to feel the hell of passion planted within me, burning until all is cold, rigid, and dead.\"}"
