          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"da7b75df6a36b14343aae77c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf I cannot live upon that, I shall not ask any man to help me along. Is that satisfactory?\u201d\\n\\nA tremendous burst of applause followed, and from its midst the king\u2019s voice rang out:\\n\\n\u201cTake off his bonds and free him! Pay him homage, all of you\u2014high and low, rich and poor\u2014for he has become the king\u2019s right hand, invested with power and authority, and his place is on the highest step of the throne! Now drive away this crawling night, and restore light and gladness, that the whole world may bless thee.\u201d\\n\\nBut I said:\\n\\n\u201cThat an ordinary man should be disgraced before the world is nothing; but it would dishonor the _king_ if those who saw his minister naked did not also see him rescued from his shame. If I might request that my clothes be returned\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey are unsuitable,\u201d the king interrupted. \u201cBring garments of another kind; dress him as a prince!\u201d\\n\\nMy scheme had succeeded. I wished to hold matters as they stood until the eclipse became total; otherwise they would begin urging me again to banish the darkness, and naturally I could not do that. Sending for the clothing bought me some time, though not enough. So I was forced to find another pretext. I said that it was only natural the king might alter his mind and partly regret what he had done in his excitement; therefore I would permit the darkness to deepen for a while, and if, after a reasonable interval, the king remained of the same mind, the darkness would be sent away. Neither the king nor anyone else liked that arrangement, but I had to stand firm.\\n\\nIt became darker and darker, blacker and blacker, while I wrestled with those clumsy sixth-century garments. At length it was utterly dark, and the crowd groaned in terror as they felt the chill, uncanny night wind moving through the place and saw the stars appear and glitter overhead. At last the eclipse was complete, and I was greatly relieved, though everyone else was miserable\u2014which was only to be expected. I said:\\n\\n\u201cThe king, through his silence, still abides by the terms.\u201d Then I raised my hands\u2014held them so for a moment\u2014and said, with the most dreadful solemnity: \u201cLet the enchantment melt away and depart without harm!\u201d\\n\\nFor a moment there was no answer in that profound darkness and sepulchral stillness. But when the sun\u2019s silver edge thrust itself forth a minute or two later, the gathering burst into a mighty cry and surged down like a flood to overwhelm me with blessings and thanks; and Clarence, certainly, was not the last wave of it.\"}"
