ners were.\\n\\nThey stayed together only a few minutes, since Miss Woodhouse must not be kept waiting. Harriet then ran to her with a smiling face and excited spirits, which Miss Woodhouse hoped soon to calm.\\n\\n\u201cOnly think of meeting him! How very strange! It was entirely by chance, he said, that he had not gone round by Randalls. He did not think we ever walked on this road. He thought we walked toward Randalls most days.\u201d\"}"
