          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"08d51f42cadbf87fe9dbb59e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon, the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away and set off at once. When they were several miles below Cave Hollow, Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, you see this bluff looks the same all the way down from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood-yards, and the bushes all look alike. But do you see that white spot up there where there\u2019s been a landslide? Well, that\u2019s one of my landmarks. We\u2019ll go ashore now.\u201d\\n\\nThey landed.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, from where we\u2019re standing, you could touch the hole I came out of with a fishing pole. See if you can find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck searched all around and found nothing. Tom proudly walked into a thick clump of sumac bushes and said:\\n\\n\u201cHere it is! Look at it, Huck; it\u2019s the coziest hole in this country. Just keep quiet about it. I\u2019ve wanted to be a robber all along, but I knew I had to have a place like this, and finding one was the trouble. We\u2019ve got it now, and we\u2019ll keep it secret. We\u2019ll only let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in\u2014because, of course, there has to be a Gang, or there wouldn\u2019t be any style to it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds splendid, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, it surely does, Tom. And who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, almost anybody. We\u2019ll waylay people\u2014that\u2019s mostly how it\u2019s done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not always. We keep them in the cave until they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them get all they can from their friends; and after you\u2019ve kept them a year, if it hasn\u2019t been raised by then, you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. Only you don\u2019t kill women. You lock up the women, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich, and terribly frightened. You 