          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"45b2a81639bd6c2a8d5c10be\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They was bringing along a very respectable-looking old gentleman, and a good-looking younger one, with his right arm tied up in a sling. And, my souls, how the crowd hollered and laughed, and wouldn\u2019t quit. But I couldn\u2019t see no fun in it, and I allowed it would be hard for the duke and king to see any. I expected they\u2019d go pale. But no, not a pale did _they_ go. The duke never showed he had any notion what was going on, but kept on goo-gooing about, pleased and contented, like a jug a-googling out buttermilk; and the king, he only stared and stared mournful at the strangers, as if it gave him a stomach-ache right in his heart to think such cheats and scoundrels could be in the world. Oh, he played it splendid. A heap of the leading people gathered round the king, to show him they stood by him. The old gentleman that had just arrived looked puzzled nearly to death. By and by he began to talk, and I noticed at once he pronounced _like_ an Englishman\u2014not in the king\u2019s fashion, though the king\u2019s was a pretty fair imitation. I can\u2019t set down the old gent\u2019s exact words, nor can I copy his way of speaking; but he turned to the crowd and said, something like this:\\n\\n\u201cThis is a surprise I wasn\u2019t prepared for; and I\u2019ll confess, open and candid, I ain\u2019t in very good shape to meet it or answer it; for my brother and I have had bad luck; he\u2019s broken his arm, and our baggage was put off at a town above here last night, through a mistake. I am Peter Wilks\u2019 brother Harvey, and this is his brother William, who can neither hear nor speak\u2014and can\u2019t even make signs worth much, now that he has only one hand to make them with. We are what we claim to be; and in a day or two, when I get the baggage, I can prove it. But till then I won\u2019t say another word, only go to the hotel and wait.\u201d\\n\\nThen he and the new dummy started away; and the king laughed, and blathered out:\\n\\n\u201cBroke his arm\u2014_very_ likely, _ain\u2019t_ it?\u2014and mighty handy, too, for a fraud that has to make signs and don\u2019t know how. Lost their baggage! That\u2019s _mighty_ fine!\u2014and mighty clever\u2014under the _circumstances!_\u201d\\n\\nThen he laughed again, and everybody else did too, except three or four, maybe half a dozen. One was that doctor; another was a keen-looking gentleman carrying an old-fashioned carpet-bag made of carpet material, who had just got off the steamboat and was speaking low to the doctor, looking toward the king now and then and nodding\u2014it was Levi Bell, the lawyer who had gone up to Louisville; and another was a large, rough, husky fellow who came up and listened to all the old gentleman said, and was listening to the king now.\"}"
