he boy instantly ran, climbed the tall board fence, and vanished over the other side.\\n\\nHis Aunt Polly stood amazed for a moment, then gave a soft laugh.\\n\\n\u201cHang that boy, can\u2019t I ever learn? Hasn\u2019t he played enough tricks on me that I ought to watch for them by now? But old fools are the biggest fools there are. You can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as they say. But goodness, he never plays the same trick two days in a row, so how is anyone supposed to know what\u2019s coming? He seems to know exactly how long he can bother me before I lose my temper, and he knows that if he can distract me for a minute or make me laugh, it all settles down again and I can\u2019t hit him a lick.\"}"
