{"request_id":"af04a6105c58594b68fcee57","rewritten_text":"“By eight o’clock, I had reached a height of seventeen miles above the earth’s surface. It was clear to me that my rate of ascent was not only increasing, but that it would have increased somewhat even if I had not thrown out the ballast I did. The pain in my head and ears returned violently at intervals, and my nose still bled now and then; but overall, I suffered far less than might have been expected. Still, I found it harder and harder to breathe, and every breath brought an unpleasant spasm in my chest. I unpacked the condensing apparatus and prepared it for immediate use.

“The view of the earth at this stage of my ascent was truly beautiful. To the west, north, and south, as far as I could see, stretched a limitless sheet of seemingly calm ocean. Every moment it grew a deeper blue and had already begun to look slightly curved. Far to the east, though still clearly visible, lay the islands of Great Britain, the whole Atlantic coasts of France and Spain, and a small part of northern Africa. Not a trace of any individual building could be seen, and mankind’s proudest cities had completely vanished from the face of the earth. From the rock of Gibraltar, now reduced to a faint speck, the dark Mediterranean, scattered with bright islands as the sky is scattered with stars, spread eastward as far as my sight could reach. At last, its vast waters seemed to plunge over the edge of the horizon, and I found myself standing on tiptoe, listening for the echoes of that mighty waterfall. Above me, the sky was black as jet, and the stars shone brilliantly.

“The pigeons seemed to be suffering greatly by this time, so I decided to set them free. I first untied one, a beautiful pigeon mottled with gray, and placed him on the edge of the wicker basket. He seemed extremely distressed, looking anxiously about, fluttering his wings, and cooing loudly, but he could not be persuaded to leave the car. At last I picked him up and threw him about six yards from the balloon. Yet instead of trying to descend, as I had expected, he struggled fiercely to return, crying out in sharp, piercing shrieks. At length he managed to regain his former place on the rim, but scarcely had he done so when his head fell upon his breast, and he dropped dead inside the car."}

