Take back your dwelling, and let me flee this place.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cFelix trembled violently as he spoke. He and his companion went into the cottage, remained there a few minutes, and then left. I never again beheld any member of the De Lacey family.\\n\\n\u201cFor the rest of the day I stayed in my hovel, sunk in complete and senseless despair. My protectors had gone, severing the sole bond that connected me with the world. For the first time, revenge and hatred possessed my breast, and I made no effort to restrain them; yielding to their current, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\"}"
