          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ddf9fbf1007a548541f55674\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJust a tick.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere\u2019d you find him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut in the woods.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t want to sell him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll right. He\u2019s a pretty small tick, anyway.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, anybody can chase down a tick that isn\u2019t theirs. I\u2019m happy with it. It\u2019s good enough for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure, there are plenty of ticks. I could get a thousand of them if I wanted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, why don\u2019t you? Because you know perfectly well you can\u2019t. This is an early tick, I guess. It\u2019s the first one I\u2019ve seen this year.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay, Huck\u2014I\u2019ll give you my tooth for him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet\u2019s see it.\u201d\\n\\nTom took out a scrap of paper and carefully unwrapped it. Huckleberry looked at it longingly. The temptation was powerful. At last he said:\\n\\n\u201cIs it real?\u201d\\n\\nTom raised his lip and showed the gap.\\n\\n\u201cWell, all right,\u201d Huckleberry said. \u201cIt\u2019s a deal.\u201d\\n\\nTom put the tick into the percussion-cap box that had recently served as the pinchbug\u2019s prison, and the boys went their separate ways, each feeling richer than before.\\n\\nWhen Tom arrived at the small, isolated wooden schoolhouse, he marched in briskly, looking like someone who had hurried there as fast as he honestly could. He hung his hat on a peg and dropped into his seat with efficient speed. The master, seated high in his large splint-bottomed armchair, had been dozing, soothed by the sleepy hum of studying. The interruption woke him.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer!\u201d\\n\\nTom knew that hearing his full name meant trouble.\\n\\n\u201cSir!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome here. Now, sir, why are you late again, as usual?\u201d\\n\\nTom was about to hide behind a lie when he saw two long yellow braids hanging down a back he recognized through love\u2019s electric sympathy; and beside that figure was the only empty seat on the girls\u2019 side of the schoolroom. He immediately said:\\n\\n\u201cI stopped to talk to Huckleberry Finn!\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s pulse seemed to stop, and he stared helplessly. The hum of study died away. The pupils wondered whether this reckless boy had lost his mind. The master said:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2014you did what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStopped to talk to Huckleberry Finn.\u201d\\n\\nThere was no misunderstanding the words.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer, this is the most astonishing confession I have ever heard. A simple ferule will not do for this offense. Take off your jacket.\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s arm continued until it was tired and the supply of switches had noticeably shrunk. Then came the command:\\n\\n\u201cNow, sir, go sit with the girls! And let this be a warning to you.\u201d\\n\\nThe titter that ran through the room seemed to embarrass the boy, but in truth he was more affected by his reverent awe of his unknown idol and the fearful delight of his extraordinary good fortune.\"}"
