          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"33ac54a8445fbf44ebc4078a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cThese thoughts soothed me, and that afternoon I fell into a deep sleep; but the fever in my blood would not let me dream peacefully. The terrible scene of the day before kept playing before my eyes: the women fleeing, and the furious Felix dragging me away from his father\u2019s feet. I woke exhausted, and, finding that night had already come, crept from my hiding place to look for food.\\n\\n\u201cWhen I had satisfied my hunger, I followed the familiar path to the cottage. Everything there was quiet. I crept into my hovel and waited silently for the usual hour when the family rose. That hour passed; the sun climbed high in the sky, but the cottagers did not appear. I shook with fear, imagining some dreadful disaster. The cottage was dark inside, and I heard no movement; I cannot describe the agony of waiting.\\n\\n\u201cSoon two countrymen passed by. They stopped near the cottage and began talking with angry gestures, but I could not understand them, because they spoke the language of the country, not that of my protectors. Shortly afterward Felix came with another man. I was surprised, for I knew he had not left the cottage that morning, and I listened anxiously, hoping his words would explain these strange events.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Do you understand,\u2019 his companion said, \u2018that you must pay three months\u2019 rent and lose the vegetables from your garden? I do not wish to treat you unfairly, and so I ask you to take a few days to consider your decision.\u2019\\n\\n\u201c\u2018It is completely useless,\u2019 Felix replied. \u2018We can never live in your cottage again. My father\u2019s life is in great danger because of the dreadful event I have told you about. My wife and sister will never recover from their terror. I beg you, do not argue with me any longer. Take back your house and let me flee this place.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cFelix shook violently as he spoke. He and his companion entered the cottage, stayed there a few minutes, and then left. I never saw any of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\n\u201cFor the rest of the day, I remained in my hovel, numb with complete despair. My protectors had gone, breaking the only bond that connected me to the world. For the first time, revenge and hatred filled my heart. I made no effort to control them; instead, carried along by their force, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\"}"
