          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f45c7e967dfab2310e2c0fb1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I then went from shop to shop, buying whatever was needed to alter his appearance. When that was done, I made my own way to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but when he saw me come in, he rose at once and stood before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. As I had walked there, I had thought carefully about what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t involve yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t involve anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything: I don\u2019t want to know anything; I am not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course, I saw that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make sure that what I have been informed is true. I have no wish for it to be untrue, but I may at least confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head and looking not at me but, as if listening, at the floor. \u201cTold would suggest spoken communication. You cannot have spoken communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who was so long unknown to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you responsible for my mistakes and false conclusions; but I had always supposed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d Mr. Jaggers replied, looking coolly at me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible for that at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it seemed so much like it, sir,\u201d I pleaded, my heart sinking.\\n\\n\u201cNot the smallest piece of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his coat-skirts. \u201cJudge nothing by appearances; judge everything by evidence. There is no better rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I said with a sigh, after standing silent for a while. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, in all my dealings with you, I have kept to the plain facts. There has never been the slightest departure from the plain facts. You know that, do you not?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhen Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014I told him that he must not expect me ever to depart from the plain facts.\u201d\"}"
