erved him well\u2014almost replacing focus and firm purpose. Thus the Spider, stubbornly watching Estella, outwaited many brighter insects, and would often uncoil himself and drop at precisely the right moment.\\n\\nAt a certain Assembly Ball in Richmond\u2014there used to be Assembly Balls in most places then\u2014where Estella had eclipsed every other beauty, this clumsy Drummle hovered around her so persistently, and with such tolerance from her, that I resolved to speak to her about him. I took the next opportunity, when she was waiting for Mrs. Blandley to take her home and sat apart among some flowers, ready to leave.\"}"
