g bathed with eau de cologne by the old housekeeper. Mr. Otis immediately insisted that she eat something and ordered supper for everyone. It was a sorrowful meal, for scarcely anyone spoke, and even the twins were shocked into quietness, being very fond of their sister. When they had finished, Mr. Otis, despite the little Duke\u2019s pleas, ordered them all to bed, saying that nothing more could be done that night and that in the morning he would telegraph Scotland Yard to send detectives at once.\"}"
