          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f83bca77fbd90f0820202f11\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Those aged and frail men were always seen by the public in the act of bowing, and people commonly believed that, after bowing one customer out, they continued bowing in the empty office until they bowed another customer in.\\n\\nThe barrister was sharp enough to see that the banker would not have stated his opinion so strongly without grounds amounting to moral certainty. Though unprepared for the large pill he had to swallow, he swallowed it. \u201cAnd now,\u201d said Mr. Stryver, once it was down, wagging his courtroom forefinger at the Temple in general, \u201cmy way out of this is to prove you all wrong.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a piece of Old Bailey strategy in which he found considerable comfort. \u201cYou shall not prove me wrong, young lady,\u201d said Mr. Stryver. \u201cI\u2019ll do that for you.\u201d\\n\\nSo, when Mr. Lorry called that evening as late as ten o\u2019clock, Mr. Stryver, surrounded by a quantity of books and papers spread out for the purpose, appeared to have nothing less on his mind than the morning\u2019s subject. He even seemed surprised to see Mr. Lorry, and was entirely distracted and preoccupied.\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d said that good-natured messenger, after a full half-hour of futile efforts to bring him back to the matter. \u201cI have been to Soho.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo Soho?\u201d Mr. Stryver repeated coolly. \u201cOh, of course! What am I thinking of?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd I have no doubt,\u201d said Mr. Lorry, \u201cthat I was right in the conversation we had. My opinion has been confirmed, and I repeat my advice.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI assure you,\u201d Mr. Stryver replied in the friendliest manner, \u201cthat I am sorry for it on your account, and sorry for it on the poor father\u2019s account. I know this must always be a painful subject for the family; let us say no more about it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t understand you,\u201d said Mr. Lorry.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say you don\u2019t,\u201d Stryver returned, nodding in a soothing, conclusive way. \u201cNever mind, never mind.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut it does matter,\u201d Mr. Lorry insisted.\\n\\n\u201cNo, it doesn\u2019t; I assure you, it doesn\u2019t. Having imagined there was sense where there is no sense, and worthy ambition where there is no worthy ambition, I am fortunate to be free of my mistake, and no harm has been done. Young women have made similar foolish mistakes many times before, and have regretted them in poverty and obscurity many times before. From an unselfish point of view, I am sorry the matter has fallen through, because it would have been a bad arrangement for me in worldly terms; from a selfish point of view, I am glad it has fallen through, because it would have been a bad arrangement for me in worldly terms\u2014it is scarcely necessary to say that I could have gained nothing by it.\u201d\"}"
