s. When they finally decided who really had seen the departed boys last and spoken the last words to them, those fortunate people took on a kind of sacred importance, while everyone else stared at them and envied them. One poor boy, with no other claim to greatness, said with fairly obvious pride:\\n\\n\u201cWell, Tom Sawyer licked me once.\u201d\\n\\nBut his attempt at glory failed. Most of the boys could say the same thing, which made the distinction too common. The group drifted away, still speaking in awed voices about memories of the lost heroes.\"}"
