obody\u2014not even the burgomaster, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk\u2014possessed the slightest clue for solving the enigma; and thus, since nothing more sensible suggested itself, every man carefully restored his pipe to the corner of his mouth and, lifting his right eye toward the apparition, puffed, paused, waddled to and fro, and grunted with significance\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and at last\u2014puffed once more.\\n\\nMeanwhile, however, the object of such curiosity, and occasion of so much smoke, descended lower and lower toward the worthy city. Within a few minutes it had come near enough to be plainly distinguished. It seemed to be\u2014yes! it was unquestionably a kind of balloon; yet surely Rotterdam had never before beheld such a balloon.\"}"
