n I!\u2014felt restored and soothed as I ate this wretched food and drank a little sour wine from a flask half full, left in that deserted habitation. Then I lay down upon the bed, which no shipwrecked sufferer need despise. The earthy scent of the dry leaves was balm to me after the loathsome smell of seaweed. I forgot my solitude. I looked neither behind nor ahead; my senses sank into rest; I slept, and dreamed of beloved inland scenes\u2014of haymakers, of a shepherd whistling to his dog when he called for help in driving the flock into fold; of the sights and sounds belonging to my mountain childhood, long since forgotten.\"}"
