          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3556840918ecdef4de3e1a9b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I next went from store to store, buying whatever was needed to alter his appearance. That errand completed, I made my way, for my own purposes, to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers sat at his desk, but on seeing me come in, rose at once and stood before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201ctake care.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. For as I came along, I had considered carefully what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t compromise yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t compromise anybody. You understand\u2014anybody. Tell me nothing: I wish to know nothing; I have no curiosity.\u201d\\n\\nNaturally, I perceived that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only wish, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make certain that what has reached me is true. I have no desire for it to prove false, but I may at least confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head and looking not at me, but toward the floor as though listening to it. \u201cTold appears to suggest spoken communication. You could not have spoken communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery good.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a man called Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who was so long unknown to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you in any way answerable for my errors and mistaken conclusions; but I had always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you observe, Pip,\u201d Mr. Jaggers returned, fixing his cool eyes on me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am in no way answerable for that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYet it seemed so much like it, sir,\u201d I urged, with my heart cast down.\\n\\n\u201cNot the smallest scrap of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and drawing together his skirts. \u201cJudge nothing by appearances; judge everything by evidence. There is no sounder rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing further to say,\u201d I said with a sigh, after I had stood quiet for a short time. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally made himself known,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, in all my dealings with you, I have kept to the exact line of fact. There has not been the slightest deviation from that exact line of fact. You are fully aware of this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFully, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI informed Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must not expect me ever to depart from the exact line of fact.\u201d\"}"
