d caused her were soon lifted, and her mind was stirred again by hopeful news that began to spread. The housekeeper at Netherfield had received orders to prepare for her master\u2019s arrival. He was coming down in a day or two to shoot there for several weeks. Mrs. Bennet was quite restless. She looked at Jane, smiled, and shook her head in turn.\\n\\n\u201cWell, well, so Mr. Bingley is coming down, sister,\u201d she said, for Mrs. Philips had brought her the news first. \u201cWell, so much the better. Not that I care about it, of course. He is nothing to us, you know, and I am sure I never wish to see him again. Still, he is very welcome to come to Netherfield, if he likes.\u201d\"}"
