          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2c5c6d82a2726a05b4299656\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, to translate the word \u2018yokel\u2019 for the ladies\u2019 benefit, I take it you mean this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d Mr. Losberne said with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s right, sir,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cThis is all concerning the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow then, what\u2019s this about the boy the servants have been talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing whatever,\u201d the doctor replied. \u201cOne of the frightened servants has taken it into his head that the boy had something to do with this attempt to break into the house; but it is nonsense\u2014utter absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasily settled, if that\u2019s so,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is perfectly true,\u201d Blathers observed, nodding in agreement and idly playing with the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he give about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the sky, did he, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor replied, casting a nervous glance at the two ladies. \u201cI know his entire history, but we can discuss that shortly. First, I suppose you would like to see where the thieves tried to get in?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d Mr. Blathers answered. \u201cWe had better inspect the premises first, then question the servants afterward. That is the usual way of conducting business.\u201d\\n\\nLights were brought, and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and, in short, everyone else, went into the small room at the end of the passage and looked out through the window. Then they went around by the lawn and looked in through it. Next, they had a candle passed outside to inspect the shutter; then a lantern to follow the footprints; and then a pitchfork to prod the bushes. When this was done, amid the breathless attention of all present, they came indoors again. Mr. Giles and Brittles were then made to give a dramatic reenactment of their parts in the previous night\u2019s events. They performed it some six times, contradicting one another in no more than one important detail the first time, and no more than a dozen by the last. Having reached this point, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a lengthy conference, whose secrecy and solemnity made a consultation among eminent doctors over the most difficult medical question seem like children\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced up and down the adjoining room in great agitation, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with anxious expressions.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after a great many rapid turns, \u201cI scarcely know what to do.\u201d\"}"
