          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ccffb55637e0e88ab0e4bea5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me closely for a moment, then said quietly,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly,\u201d I said, \u201cthat you will not confuse them with the others. They may be of the same blood, but believe me, they are not of the same kind.\u201d\\n\\nStill watching me closely, Miss Havisham repeated,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou see, I am not clever enough,\u201d I replied, feeling myself blush a little, \u201cto hide from you, even if I wished to, that I do want something. Miss Havisham, if you would give the money to do my friend Herbert a lasting good in life, though it must, by its nature, be done without his knowing, I could tell you how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy must it be done without his knowledge?\u201d she asked, placing her hands on her stick so that she could look at me more closely.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began helping him myself more than two years ago, without his knowledge, and I do not want to be discovered. Why I am unable to finish it, I cannot explain. That is part of a secret belonging to someone else, not to me.\u201d\\n\\nShe slowly took her eyes from me and turned them toward the fire. She watched it in silence for what seemed, by the dim light of the candles burning down, a long time. Then some red coals fell apart, and she looked at me again\u2014at first blankly, then with attention that slowly sharpened. All this time Estella went on knitting. When Miss Havisham had fixed her attention on me, she said, as though our conversation had never paused,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to control my shaking voice, \u201cyou know that I love you. You know that I have loved you deeply and for a long time.\u201d\\n\\nAt my words, she lifted her eyes to my face. Her fingers continued their work, and she looked at me without any