          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"35da785dc6f2b36f29d59130\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect\u2019s weight was quite remarkable, and, all things considered, I could scarcely blame Jupiter for his opinion of it; but what to make of Legrand\u2019s agreement with that opinion, I could not for the life of me understand.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said in a lofty tone, after I had finished examining the beetle, \u201cI sent for you so that I might have your advice and help in carrying out the designs of Fate and of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I cried, cutting him off, \u201cyou are certainly unwell and ought to take some precautions. You must go to bed, and I will stay with you for a few days, until you recover. You are feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did so and, to tell the truth, found not the slightest sign of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut you may be ill without having a fever. Let me prescribe for you this once. First, go to bed. Then\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are mistaken,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cI am as well as I can be, considering the excitement I am under. If you truly wish me well, you will help relieve that excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how is that to be done?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and we will need the assistance of someone we can trust. You are the only person we can rely on. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me now will be equally calmed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am eager to oblige you in any way,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut do you mean to say that this cursed beetle has something to do with your expedition into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can take no part in such an absurd undertaking.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am sorry\u2014very sorry\u2014for we shall have to attempt it alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAttempt it alone! The man is surely mad! But wait\u2014how long do you intend to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMost likely all night. We will leave at once and, in any case, return by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me, on your honor, that when this whim of yours is over, and the business of the bug\u2014good God!\u2014has been settled to your satisfaction, you will return home and follow my advice exactly, as your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise; and now let us go, for we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I went with my friend. We set out at about four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and I. Jupiter carried the scythe and the spades, all of which he insisted on bearing himself\u2014apparently less from unusual diligence or willingness than from fear of allowing any of the tools to remain within his master\u2019s reach.\"}"
