ss, \u201cI must ask you what you mean by this.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d said Biddy.\\n\\n\u201cNow, don\u2019t repeat me,\u201d I replied. \u201cYou did not used to repeat me, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid not used to!\u201d said Biddy. \u201cOh, Mr. Pip! Used to!\u201d\\n\\nWell, I thought I had better give up that point too. After another silent walk through the garden, I returned to the main matter.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, \u201cI remarked that I would come down here often to see Joe, and you received it with a noticeable silence. Please tell me, Biddy, why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite sure, then, that you WILL come to see him often?\u201d Biddy asked, stopping in the narrow garden path and looking at me beneath the stars with clear, honest eyes.\"}"
