          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"41d9d476b16b5b668caf0d50\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut do not suppose I did not think it was wrong in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBelieve me, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPerhaps that would not make me like them any better. So many women and children have no right to be comfortable on board a ship.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you are talking nonsense. Pray, what would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to be carried from one port to another to follow our husbands, if everyone felt as you do?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy feelings, as you see, did not stop me from taking Mrs Harville and all her family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I hate to hear you speak like such a grand gentleman, as though women were all delicate ladies instead of sensible creatures. None of us expect calm seas every day of our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has a wife, he will change his tune. Once he is married, if we are lucky enough to live through another war, we shall see him do what you and I, and many others, have done. He will be very grateful to anyone who brings his wife to him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, he will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I am finished,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cOnce married people begin attacking me with, \u2018Oh, you will think very differently when you are married,\u2019 I can only say, \u2018No, I will not\u2019; then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that ends the matter.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and walked away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cFairly well, ma\u2019am, during my fifteen years of marriage, though many women have travelled more. I have crossed the Atlantic four times, and gone once to the East Indies and back; besides visiting various places nearer home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Straits, and never visited the West Indies. We do not count Bermuda or the Bahamas, you know, as the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to say against this; in all her life, she could not accuse herself of having called them anything at all.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft continued, \u201cnothing can be more comfortable than a man-of-war; I mean, of the larger kinds. On a frigate, of course, you are more cramped, though any sensible woman can be perfectly happy in one. I can safely say that the happiest part of my life has been spent aboard a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\"}"
