          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0876a722caf7debaeb6c2fc2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIt is a strange thing, but everyone who vanishes is said to have been seen in San Francisco. It must be a wonderful city, with all the attractions of the next world.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you think happened to Basil?\u201d Dorian asked, raising his Burgundy to the light and wondering how he could speak of it so calmly.\\n\\n\u201cI have no idea. If Basil has chosen to hide, that is not my concern. If he is dead, I do not want to think of him. Death is the only thing that truly frightens me. I hate it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy?\u201d the younger man asked wearily.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d said Lord Henry, holding the gold lattice of an open vinaigrette box beneath his nose, \u201cthese days one can survive anything except that. Death and vulgarity are the only two facts of the nineteenth century that cannot be explained away. Let us have coffee in the music-room, Dorian. You must play Chopin for me. The man my wife ran away with played Chopin beautifully. Poor Victoria! I was very fond of her. The house is rather lonely without her. Of course, married life is only a habit\u2014a bad habit. Yet one regrets losing even one\u2019s worst habits. Perhaps one regrets them most of all. They are such an important part of one\u2019s personality.\u201d\\n\\nDorian said nothing. He rose from the table, went into the next room, sat at the piano, and let his fingers wander over the black and white ivory keys. When the coffee was brought in, he stopped and looked at Lord Henry. \u201cHarry, has it ever occurred to you that Basil was murdered?\u201d\\n\\nLord Henry yawned. \u201cBasil was very popular, and he always wore a Waterbury watch. Why would anyone murder him? He was not clever enough to make enemies. Certainly, he had great genius as a painter. But a man may paint like Velasquez and still be as dull as possible. Basil was really rather dull. He interested me only once: years ago, when he told me he adored you wildly, and that you were the main inspiration for his art.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI was very fond of Basil,\u201d Dorian said, with sadness in his voice. \u201cBut do people not say that he was murdered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, some newspapers do. It does not seem likely to me. I know there are terrible places in Paris, but Basil was not the kind of man who would go to them. He had no curiosity. That was his chief fault.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would you say, Harry, if I told you that I murdered Basil?\u201d asked the younger man.\"}"
