          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a7cf6a376804a626d0aee041\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This was Mrs. Umney, the housekeeper, whom Mrs. Otis had agreed to retain in her former post at Lady Canterville\u2019s urgent request. She gave each of them a deep curtsey as they stepped down from the carriage, and said in a quaint, old-fashioned way, \u2018Welcome to Canterville Chase.\u2019 They followed her through the splendid Tudor hall into the library, a long, low room panelled in black oak, with a large stained-glass window at one end. Tea had been set out there, and after removing their wraps, they sat down and began looking about the room while Mrs. Umney attended them.\\n\\nSuddenly Mrs. Otis noticed a dull red stain on the floor beside the fireplace and, having no idea what it truly meant, said to Mrs. Umney, \u2018I\u2019m afraid something has been spilled there.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, madam,\u2019 the old housekeeper replied quietly, \u2018blood was spilled on that spot.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018How dreadful!\u2019 cried Mrs. Otis. \u2018I certainly do not want bloodstains in a sitting-room. It must be removed immediately.\u2019\\n\\nThe old woman smiled and answered in the same hushed, mysterious voice, \u2018It is the blood of Lady Eleanore de Canterville, murdered on that very spot by her own husband, Sir Simon de Canterville, in 1575. Sir Simon outlived her by nine years, then vanished suddenly in very mysterious circumstances. His body has never been found, but his guilty spirit still haunts the Chase. The bloodstain has been greatly admired by tourists and others, and cannot be removed.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018That is complete nonsense,\u2019 cried Washington Otis. \u2018Pinkerton\u2019s Champion Stain Remover and Paragon Detergent will take it out in no time.\u2019 Before the terrified housekeeper could stop him, he had dropped to his knees and was briskly scrubbing the floor with a small stick of something that looked like black cosmetic. Within minutes, not a trace of the bloodstain remained.\\n\\n\u2018I knew Pinkerton would do it,\u2019 he said triumphantly, looking around at his admiring family. But the moment he spoke, a terrible flash of lightning illuminated the gloomy room, a dreadful crash of thunder made them all leap to their feet, and Mrs. Umney fainted.\\n\\n\u2018What an appalling climate!\u2019 said the American Minister calmly, lighting a long cheroot. \u2018I suppose the old country is so overcrowded that there isn\u2019t enough decent weather for everyone. I have always believed emigration is England\u2019s only solution.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear Hiram,\u2019 cried Mrs. Otis, \u2018what are we to do with a woman who faints?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Charge her for it, like breakages,\u2019 the Minister replied. \u2018She won\u2019t faint again after that.\u2019 And within a few moments, Mrs. Umney did indeed recover.\"}"
