Everything else, at least in imagination, went perfectly smoothly. All the smaller details of tables and chairs, lights and music, tea and supper, seemed to arrange themselves, or were left as little matters to be settled later by Mrs. Weston and Mrs. Stokes.\u2014Everyone invited was certain to come; Frank had already written to Enscombe to ask to stay a few days beyond his fortnight, and that could not possibly be refused. It was going to be a delightful dance.\\n\\nWhen Miss Bates arrived, she warmly agreed that it must be. They did not need her as an adviser; but as someone to approve, a much safer role, she was truly welcome. Her approval, both broad and detailed, warm and unending, could only please them; and for another half-hour they all walked back and forth between the rooms, some making suggestions, some listening, and all happily enjoying the prospect before them.\"}"
