          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ee36d475c9d03c03d1ff594e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me closely for a moment, then said quietly,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly,\u201d I said, \u201cthat you will not confuse them with the others. They may be of the same blood, but believe me, they are not of the same nature.\u201d\\n\\nStill watching me intently, Miss Havisham repeated,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am not clever enough, you see,\u201d I replied, aware that I blushed a little, \u201cto conceal from you, even if I wished to, that I do want something. Miss Havisham, if you would provide the money to do my friend Herbert a lasting service in life\u2014a service which, by its nature, must be done without his knowing\u2014I could tell you how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy must it be done without his knowledge?\u201d she asked, placing both hands on her stick so that she could look at me more closely.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began the service myself more than two years ago, without his knowledge, and I do not want to be exposed. Why I am unable to complete it, I cannot explain. That is part of a secret belonging to someone else, not to me.\u201d\\n\\nGradually she took her eyes from me and turned them toward the fire. She watched it for what, in the silence and by the dimming light of the slowly burning candles, seemed a long time. Then the fall of some red coals startled her, and she looked at me again\u2014at first blankly, then with attention that slowly gathered and fixed itself. All this while Estella continued knitting. When Miss Havisham had fully fixed her attention on me, she said, as though our conversation had never paused,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWhat else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to steady my trembling voice, \u201cyou know that I love you. You know I have loved you deeply and for a long time.\u201d\\n\\nAt my address, she lifted her eyes to my face. Her fingers continued their work, and she looked at me without any change of expression. I saw Miss Havisham glance from me to her, and from her back to me.\\n\\n\u201cI would have said this sooner, if not for my long mistake. It led me to hope that Miss Havisham intended us for each other. While I believed that you could not help yourself, in a way, I held back from saying it. But I must say it now.\u201d\\n\\nWithout changing her expression, her fingers still moving, Estella shook her head.\\n\\n\u201cI know,\u201d I said in response to that gesture. \u201cI know. I have no hope that I will ever call you mine, Estella.\u201d\"}"
