          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7c196d5c28788874a73bb245\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStop the starboard! Ting-a-ling-ling! Stop the larboard! Come ahead on the starboard! Stop her! Let your outside wheel turn slowly! Ting-a-ling-ling! Chow-ow-ow! Get out that head-line! Lively now! Come\u2014get out your spring-line\u2014what are you doing there? Take a turn around that stump with the bight of it! Stand by that stage now\u2014let her go! Engines stopped, sir! Ting-a-ling-ling! SH\u2019T! S\u2019H\u2019T! SH\u2019T!\u201d (testing the gauge-cocks).\\n\\nTom kept whitewashing and paid no attention to the steamboat. Ben stared for a moment, then said: \u201cHi-Yi! You\u2019re stuck, aren\u2019t you!\u201d\\n\\nNo answer. Tom looked over his latest stroke like an artist, then gave the brush another light sweep and studied the result again. Ben came up beside him. Tom\u2019s mouth watered for the apple, but he kept working. Ben said:\\n\\n\u201cHello, old fellow, you have to work, eh?\u201d\\n\\nTom turned suddenly and said:\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s you, Ben! I didn\u2019t notice.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay\u2014I\u2019m going swimming. Don\u2019t you wish you could come? But of course you\u2019d rather work, wouldn\u2019t you? Of course you would!\u201d\\n\\nTom looked at the boy for a moment and said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you call work?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, isn\u2019t that work?\u201d\\n\\nTom went on whitewashing and answered casually:\\n\\n\u201cWell, maybe it is, and maybe it isn\u2019t. All I know is, Tom Sawyer likes it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, come on\u2014you don\u2019t mean to say you like it?\u201d\\n\\nThe brush kept moving.\\n\\n\u201cLike it? Well, why shouldn\u2019t I? Does a boy get the chance to whitewash a fence every day?\u201d\\n\\nThat made Ben see it differently. He stopped biting his apple. Tom moved his brush carefully back and forth, stepped back to judge the effect, added a touch here and there, and judged it again. Ben watched every move, growing more interested and absorbed. At last he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let me whitewash a little.\u201d\\n\\nTom thought it over and was about to agree, but then changed his mind:\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I don\u2019t think it would do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly is terribly particular about this fence\u2014right here by the street, you know. If it were the back fence, I wouldn\u2019t mind, and neither would she. Yes, she\u2019s very particular about this fence. It has to be done very carefully. I don\u2019t suppose one boy in a thousand\u2014maybe two thousand\u2014could do it the way it has to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that true? Oh, come on, let me try. Just a little. I\u2019d let you, if you were me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honest; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn\u2019t let him. Sid wanted to do it too, and she wouldn\u2019t let Sid.\u201d\"}"
