          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ca758293ec29416f2aa22703\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, to explain the word yokel for the ladies, I take you to mean that this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s right, master,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cThen what\u2019s this about the boy the servants are talking about?\u201d asked Blathers.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d replied the doctor. \u201cOne of the frightened servants has got it into his head that the boy had something to do with the attempt to break into the house; but it is nonsense\u2014complete absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough to settle, if it is,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is quite right,\u201d Blathers observed, nodding and carelessly playing with the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he give about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor replied, glancing nervously at the two ladies. \u201cI know his whole history, but we can discuss that later. First, I suppose you would like to see the place where the thieves tried to get in?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d said Mr. Blathers. \u201cWe had better inspect the house first, and question the servants afterward. That is the usual way of doing things.\u201d\\n\\nLights were brought, and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and everyone else, went into the little room at the end of the passage and looked out through the window. Then they went around by the lawn and looked in through it. Next, someone handed out a candle so they could inspect the shutter; then a lantern to follow the footprints; and then a pitchfork to poke through the bushes. When this was done, while everyone watched with breathless interest, they came inside again. Mr. Giles and Brittles were made to act out their parts in the previous night\u2019s events, which they did about six times, contradicting each other in no more than one important detail the first time, and no more than a dozen by the last. Once this had been achieved, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a long private discussion, so secret and solemn that a meeting of great doctors over the most difficult medical question would have seemed like child\u2019s play beside it.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced up and down the next room in great uneasiness, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched him anxiously.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after many quick turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
