          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1ddfbae699fdc0c4a35f2edc\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I was sorry to hear Jim say that; it brought him down so low. My conscience began troubling me worse than ever, until finally I said to it, \u201cLeave me alone\u2014it isn\u2019t too late yet\u2014I\u2019ll paddle ashore at first light and tell.\u201d Right away I felt calm and happy and light as a feather. All my troubles were gone. I began watching closely for a light, and singing a little to myself. Before long, one appeared. Jim called out:\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019s safe, Huck, we\u2019s safe! Get up and kick your heels! That\u2019s good old Cairo at last\u2014I just know it!\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll take the canoe and go see, Jim. It might not be, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHe jumped up and made the canoe ready, put his old coat in the bottom for me to sit on, and handed me the paddle. As I pushed off, he said:\\n\\n\u201cPretty soon I\u2019ll be shouting for joy, and I\u2019ll say it was all because of Huck; I\u2019s a free man, and I never could have been free if it hadn\u2019t been for Huck; Huck done it. Jim won\u2019t ever forget you, Huck; you\u2019s the best friend Jim ever had; and you\u2019s the only friend old Jim has now.\u201d\\n\\nI was paddling away, sweating all over to turn him in; but when he said that, it seemed to take all the heart out of me. I went along slowly then, and wasn\u2019t quite sure whether I was glad I had started or not. When I was fifty yards away, Jim said:\\n\\n\u201cThere you goes, the old true Huck; the only white gentleman that ever kept his promise to old Jim.\u201d\\n\\nWell, I felt sick. But I said, I have to do it\u2014I can\u2019t get out of it. Just then a skiff came along with two men in it carrying guns. They stopped, and I stopped. One of them said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that over there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA piece of a raft,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cDo you belong on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAny men on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly one, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, five Black men ran off tonight up above the head of the bend. Is your man white or Black?\u201d\\n\\nI didn\u2019t answer right away. I tried, but the words would not come. For a second or two I tried to steady myself and say it, but I wasn\u2019t man enough\u2014I hadn\u2019t the courage of a rabbit. I saw I was giving way, so I stopped trying and said:\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s white.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose we\u2019ll go see for ourselves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI wish you would,\u201d I said, \u201cbecause it\u2019s Pap there, and maybe you could help me tow the raft ashore where the light is.\u201d\"}"
