          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d81a64a37a6a07b572f89d21\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cApril 12th. A remarkable change occurred in the balloon\u2019s direction, and though I had fully expected it, it gave me the clearest delight. Having reached, on its former course, about the twentieth parallel of south latitude, it suddenly turned at a sharp angle eastward, and continued so throughout the day, remaining nearly, if not entirely, in the exact plane of the lunar ellipse. Notably, this change of course caused a very perceptible swaying of the car\u2014a swaying that persisted, to a greater or lesser extent, for many hours.\\n\\n\u201cApril 13th. I was again greatly alarmed by a repetition of the loud crackling sound that had terrified me on the tenth. I considered the matter for a long time, but could reach no satisfactory conclusion. The earth\u2019s apparent diameter had greatly diminished; from the balloon it now subtended an angle of little more than twenty-five degrees. The moon was entirely invisible, being nearly at my zenith. I still remained in the plane of the ellipse, but made little eastward progress.\\n\\n\u201cApril 14th. The earth\u2019s diameter diminished with extreme rapidity. Today I became strongly convinced that the balloon was actually traveling up the line of apsides toward the point of perigee\u2014in other words, following the direct course that would bring it immediately to the moon at that point in its orbit nearest the earth. The moon itself was directly overhead and therefore concealed from my sight. Great and prolonged effort was required to condense the atmosphere.\\n\\n\u201cApril 15th. Even the outlines of continents and seas could no longer be distinguished on the earth with anything like clarity. At about twelve o\u2019clock, I heard for the third time that dreadful sound which had so astonished me before. This time, however, it lasted for several moments and grew louder as it continued. At last, while I stood stunned and terrified, expecting I knew not what horrible destruction, the car shook with tremendous violence, and a gigantic flaming mass of some substance I could not identify rushed past the balloon, roaring and booming with the voice of a thousand thunders. When my fear and astonishment had somewhat subsided, I had little difficulty in believing it to be some immense volcanic fragment hurled from the world I was approaching so rapidly, and most likely one of that strange class of objects occasionally found on earth and called meteoric stones for lack of a better name.\\n\\n\u201cApril 16th. Today, looking upward as best I could through each side window in turn, I saw, to my great delight, a very small portion of the moon\u2019s disk appearing, as if on every side, beyond the balloon\u2019s enormous circumference.\"}"
