\\n\\nShe stopped for a few moments. Emma could not speak.\\n\\n\u201cI do not wonder, Miss Woodhouse,\u201d she continued, \u201cthat you should see such a great difference between the two, whether in relation to me or to anyone. You must think one five hundred million times more above me than the other. But I hope, Miss Woodhouse, supposing\u2014that if\u2014strange as it may seem\u2014. You know those were your own words: that more extraordinary things had happened, that matches with greater differences in rank had taken place than one between Mr. Frank Churchill and me. So it seems that even something like this may have happened before\u2014and if I should be fortunate beyond all expression enough to\u2014if Mr. Knightley really should\u2014if he does not mind the difference between us, I hope, dear Miss Woodhouse, you will not oppose it or try to place obstacles in the way.\u201d\"}"
