lutching the table leg with hands and feet, I watched the miserable creature play with his glass, lift it, smile, throw back his head, and swallow the brandy. Immediately afterward, the company was seized with unspeakable alarm when he sprang to his feet, spun around several times in a horrifying, spasmodic whooping-cough dance, and rushed out through the door. Then he appeared at the window, plunging about and spitting violently, making the most dreadful faces and seeming completely out of his mind.\\n\\nI held on tightly while Mrs. Joe and Joe ran to him.\"}"
