          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9c9c1b775364647e69661952\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner, the whole gang went out to hunt turtle eggs on the sandbar. They poked sticks into the sand, and whenever they found a soft spot, they knelt down and dug with their hands. Sometimes they took fifty or sixty eggs from one hole. They were perfectly round and white, a little smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a grand feast of fried eggs, and another on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast, they went shouting and leaping out onto the sandbar. They chased one another round and round, throwing off clothes as they ran, until they were naked. Then they carried on farther up into the shallow water, fighting the strong current, which kept knocking their legs out from under them and made the game even more fun. Every now and then they gathered together and splashed water into each other\u2019s faces with their hands. They edged closer, turning their faces away from the choking spray, until at last they grabbed and wrestled, and the stronger boy ducked the other. Then all of them went under in a tangle of white arms and legs and came up blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath all at once.\\n\\nWhen they were thoroughly tired, they ran out and stretched themselves on the dry, hot sand. They lay there, covering themselves with it, and after a while rushed back into the water to repeat the whole performance. At last they decided their bare skin looked enough like flesh-colored tights, so they drew a ring in the sand and put on a circus\u2014with three clowns, because none of them would give up that proudest role to another.\\n\\nNext they brought out their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until that, too, became dull. Then Joe and Huck went swimming again, but Tom would not risk it. When he had kicked off his trousers, he discovered that he had also kicked the string of rattlesnake rattles from his ankle.