          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1d6e096f6a6389798f0b5aba\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Certainly, he was very entertaining, and so forth, but I was terribly disappointed; and when I questioned him about the coat of mail, he merely laughed, saying that England was much too cold a country in which to wear it. Ah, here comes Mr. Podgers! Mr. Podgers, I want you to read the Duchess of Paisley\u2019s hand. Duchess, you must remove your glove. No, not the left hand\u2014the other one.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Gladys, I really cannot think it quite proper,\u2019 said the Duchess, weakly undoing the buttons of a somewhat dirty kid glove.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing that is interesting ever is,\u2019 said Lady Windermere: \u2018_on a fait le monde ainsi_. But I must present you. Duchess, this is Mr. Podgers, my favourite cheiromantist. Mr. Podgers, this is the Duchess of Paisley; and if you declare that her mountain of the moon is larger than mine, I shall never trust you again.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am quite sure, Gladys, that there is nothing of that sort in my hand,\u2019 observed the Duchess solemnly.\\n\\n\u2018Your Grace is perfectly correct,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, looking at the small plump hand and its short, square fingers; \u2018the mountain of the moon is undeveloped. The life-line, however, is excellent. Will you kindly bend the wrist? Thank you. Three clear lines on the _rascette_! You will reach a very great age, Duchess, and be exceedingly happy. Ambition\u2014quite moderate, line of intellect not overmarked, line of heart\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Now do be indiscreet, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing could please me more,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, with a bow, \u2018if the Duchess had ever been so; but I regret to say that I perceive a great constancy of affection, joined to a strong feeling of duty.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Please continue, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 said the Duchess, appearing highly gratified.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is by no means the smallest of your Grace\u2019s virtues,\u2019 Mr. Podgers went on, and Lady Windermere burst into peals of laughter.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is an excellent thing,\u2019 said the Duchess complacently; \u2018when I married Paisley, he possessed eleven castles and not one house fit to inhabit.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And now he possesses twelve houses and not one castle,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Well, my dear,\u2019 said the Duchess, \u2018I prefer\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Comfort,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018with modern conveniences, and hot water supplied to every bedroom. Your Grace is quite right. Comfort is the sole thing civilisation can offer us.\\n\\n\u2018You have described the Duchess\u2019s character wonderfully, Mr. Podgers, and now you must tell Lady Flora\u2019s\u2019; and, in response to a nod from the smiling hostess, a tall girl with sandy Scottish hair and prominent shoulder-blades came awkwardly out from behind the sofa and extended a long, bony hand with spatulate fingers.\\n\\n\u2018Ah, a pianist, I perceive,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018a very fine pianist, though perhaps scarcely a musician.\u2019\"}"
