d come in and do everything he could for little Hello-Central. And that is what he did. He tossed his helmet into a corner, and within half a minute had put a fresh wick in the alcohol lamp and was heating the croup-kettle. By then Sandy had made a blanket canopy over the crib, and all was ready.\\n\\nSir Launcelot raised the steam. He and I filled the kettle with unslaked lime and carbolic acid, adding a little lactic acid, then filled it with water and put the steam-spout beneath the canopy. Everything was in order now, and we sat on opposite sides of the crib to keep watch.\"}"
