          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"146a82392de37f0d5158c90c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the centre of this opening I noticed a white object, though at first I could not tell what it was. Altering the telescope\u2019s focus, I looked once more, and then recognized it as a human skull.\\n\\n\u201cOn making this discovery, I was confident that I had solved the riddle; for the words \u2018main branch, seventh limb, east side,\u2019 could mean nothing but the skull\u2019s place in the tree, while \u2018shoot from the left eye of the death\u2019s head\u2019 likewise allowed only one construction in connection with a hunt for hidden treasure. I saw that the intention was to let a bullet fall from the skull\u2019s left eye, and that a bee-line\u2014that is, a straight line\u2014drawn from the nearest point of the trunk through \u2018the shot,\u2019 or the place where the bullet struck, and continued fifty feet beyond, would mark a certain spot; and beneath that spot I considered it at least possible that some valuable deposit was hidden.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll this,\u201d said I, \u201cis perfectly plain, and though ingenious, is nevertheless simple and definite. What did you do after leaving the Bishop\u2019s Hotel?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, after carefully noting the tree\u2019s bearings, I set out for home. Yet the moment I quitted \u2018the devil\u2019s seat,\u2019 the round opening disappeared, and afterward I could not catch sight of it, however I turned. What appears to me the greatest ingenuity in the entire affair is the fact\u2014for repeated trials have persuaded me that it is indeed a fact\u2014that this circular aperture can be seen from no other accessible viewpoint than the narrow shelf on the rock\u2019s face.\\n\\n\u201cOn this visit to the \u2018Bishop\u2019s Hotel,\u2019 Jupiter accompanied me. He had doubtless noticed, during the preceding weeks, my absent manner, and was especially careful not to let me out of his sight. But the following day, rising very early, I managed to evade him and went into the hills to seek the tree. After considerable labor, I found it. When I returned home that evening, my valet offered to flog me. The remainder of the adventure, I believe, you know as well as I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI presume,\u201d I said, \u201cthat in your first attempt to dig, you missed the place because of Jupiter\u2019s stupidity in allowing the bug to drop through the skull\u2019s right eye rather than its left.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly. That blunder caused a difference of about two and a half inches in \u2018the shot\u2019\u2014that is, in the position of the peg nearest the tree. Had the treasure lain directly beneath \u2018the shot,\u2019 the mistake would have mattered little; but \u2018the shot,\u2019 along with the nearest point of the tree, served merely as two points for fixing a line of direction. Naturally, the error, slight though it was at the outset, grew as we followed the line, and by the time we had gone fifty feet, it had led us wholly astray.\u201d\"}"
