          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e0eea29448600d0dec5ca338\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u2018Good heavens!\u2019 the Duchess said to herself. \u2018So he is some kind of chiropodist after all. How dreadful. I hope, at least, that he is a foreigner. That would not be quite so bad.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I really must introduce him to you.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Introduce him!\u2019 cried the Duchess. \u2018You don\u2019t mean he is here?\u2019 She began searching for a small tortoiseshell fan and a very worn lace shawl, so that she could leave at a moment\u2019s notice.\\n\\n\u2018Of course he is here. I would never think of giving a party without him. He says I have a perfectly psychic hand, and that if my thumb were the slightest bit shorter, I would be a confirmed pessimist and have entered a convent.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, I understand!\u2019 said the Duchess, greatly relieved. \u2018He tells fortunes, I suppose?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And misfortunes too,\u2019 Lady Windermere replied, \u2018as many as you like. Next year, for example, I am in terrible danger both on land and at sea, so I intend to live in a balloon and have my dinner hauled up in a basket every evening. It is all written on my little finger, or in the palm of my hand\u2014I forget which.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018But surely that is tempting Providence, Gladys.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear Duchess, surely Providence has learned to resist temptation by now. I think everyone ought to have their hands read once a month, just to know what not to do. Naturally, one does it anyway, but it is so pleasant to be warned. Now, unless someone fetches Mr. Podgers immediately, I shall have to go myself.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Let me go, Lady Windermere,\u2019 said a tall, handsome young man standing nearby, listening with an amused smile.\\n\\n\u2018Thank you so much, Lord Arthur, but I am afraid you would not recognise him.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018If he is as remarkable as you say, Lady Windermere, I can hardly fail to spot him. Tell me what he looks like