          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0d552cdf578373a7fd6d67b6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNever!\u201d the girl replied.\\n\\n\u201cTell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFor one reason,\u201d the girl answered firmly, \u201cone reason the lady knows of and will support me in\u2014I know she will, because she has promised me. And for another reason: however bad a life he has lived, I have lived a bad life too. Many of us have followed the same path together, and I will not betray them. Any one of them might have betrayed me, but they did not, bad as they are.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d said the gentleman quickly, as though this were the point he had been trying to reach, \u201cput Monks into my hands, and leave me to deal with him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat if he betrays the others?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI promise you that, if the truth is forced from him, it will end there. There must be circumstances in Oliver\u2019s early history that would be painful to expose to the public; and once the truth is brought out, they shall go free.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd if it is not?\u201d the girl asked.\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d the gentleman continued, \u201cthis Fagin shall not be brought to justice without your consent. In that event, I think I could show you reasons that would persuade you to give it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo I have the lady\u2019s promise for that?\u201d asked the girl.\\n\\n\u201cYou do,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cMy honest and faithful pledge.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMonks would never find out how you came to know what you know?\u201d said the girl, after a brief pause.\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d replied the gentleman. \u201cThe information would be used against him in such a way that he could not even guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been a liar, and lived among liars, since I was a little child,\u201d said the girl after another silence, \u201cbut I will trust your words.\u201d\\n\\nAfter receiving assurance from them both that she could safely do so, she began, in a voice so low that the listener often found it hard even to make out her meaning, to describe by name and location the public house from which she had been followed that night. From the way he occasionally paused, it seemed that the gentleman was making hurried notes of the information she gave him. When she had fully explained the layout of the place, the best spot from which to watch it without attracting notice, and the night and hour when Monks most often visited it, she paused for a few moments, apparently trying to recall his face and appearance more clearly.\\n\\n\u201cHe is tall,\u201d said the girl, \u201cand strongly built, but not heavy; he walks furtively, and as he walks he is always looking over his shoulder, first to one side and then to the other.\u201d\"}"
