her\u2019s abdication. In this she failed. The stories he received, however distorted, of a great and wise nation claiming its right to govern itself stirred his admiration; while still young, he became a republican by conviction. Yet his mother did not lose hope. To a love of authority and the proud awareness of his birth, she added firm ambition, patience, and self-command. She devoted herself to studying her son\u2019s character. Through praise, blame, and persuasion, she tried to find and strike the right notes; and though the music that answered her touch sounded like discord to her, she placed her hopes in his talents and believed she would eventually win him over.\"}"
