          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8da34f7e91698fbe118d44bf\",\"rewritten_text\":\"All at once Mr. Podgers let go of Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand and caught his left, stooping so close over it that the gold edges of his spectacles appeared almost to graze the palm. For an instant his face was a pale mask of terror; then he quickly regained his _sang-froid_, and, glancing up at Lady Windermere, remarked with an uneasy smile, \u2018It is the hand of a delightful young man.\\n\\n\u2018Naturally it is!\u2019 replied Lady Windermere, \u2018but will he make a delightful husband? That is what I wish to know.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018All delightful young men do,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u2018I do not think a husband ought to be excessively fascinating,\u2019 Lady Jedburgh observed thoughtfully, \u2018it is so perilous.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear child, they never are excessively fascinating,\u2019 exclaimed Lady Windermere. \u2018But I want particulars. Particulars are the only things that matter. What is to happen to Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, during the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh yes, his honeymoon, naturally!\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And lose a relation.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not his sister, I trust?\u2019 asked Lady Jedburgh, in a mournful voice.\\n\\n\u2018Certainly not his sister,\u2019 Mr. Podgers answered, making a protesting gesture with his hand, \u2018only a distant relation.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, I am terribly disappointed,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018I have positively nothing to tell Sybil to-morrow. Nobody cares for distant relations nowadays. They became unfashionable years ago. Still, I suppose she had better keep a black silk ready; it always serves for church, you know. And now let us have supper. They will certainly have consumed everything, but perhaps we may discover some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois once made excellent soup, but he is so disturbed by politics just now that I never feel entirely sure of him. I do wish General Boulanger would be quiet. Duchess, I am certain you must be tired?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not in the least, dear Gladys,\u2019 replied the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have enjoyed myself enormously, and the cheiropodist\u2014I mean the cheiromantist\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where can my tortoise-shell fan be? Oh, thank you so much, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind, I am sure\u2019; and the good creature at last succeeded in getting downstairs without dropping her scent-bottle more than twice.\\n\\nThroughout all this Lord Arthur Savile had stood beside the fireplace, oppressed by the same dread, the same nauseating conviction of approaching evil. He gave his sister a sad smile as she passed him on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, beautiful in her pink brocade and pearls, and scarcely heard Lady Windermere call for him to come after her. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the thought that anything might separate them brought tears dimly into his eyes.\"}"
