          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"fb3c8d93febd3312fc89d13c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"From the stairs where we had put him aboard, and ever since, I had watched carefully for any sign that we were suspected. I had seen none. We certainly had not been, and at that moment we certainly were not, watched or followed by any boat. If any boat had been waiting for us, I should have steered toward shore and forced it either to pass on or reveal its purpose. But we continued on our way without any sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and looked, as I have said, like a natural part of the scene. It was remarkable\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he had lived explained it\u2014that he was less anxious than any of us. He was not unconcerned, for he told me he hoped to live to see his gentleman become one of the finest gentlemen in a foreign country. Nor was he ready to submit or give up, as I understood him; but he had no wish to go looking for danger. When danger came to him, he faced it, but he would not trouble himself before it did.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knowed, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here alongside my dear boy and have my smoke, after being shut up day after day between four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the pleasures of freedom,\u201d I replied.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head seriously. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it like I do. You must have been under lock and key, dear boy, to know it like I do\u2014but I ain\u2019t going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt seemed inconsistent to me that, for any great purpose, he should have risked his freedom and even his life. But I reflected that freedom without danger might have been so unlike everything he had known that it could not mean to him what it would mean to another man. I was not far wrong, for after smoking a while, he said:\u2014\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, on the other side of the world, I was always looking toward this side; and being there felt empty, though I was growing rich. Everybody knowed Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody would trouble their heads about him. They ain\u2019t so easy about me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, anyway, if they knowed where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou will be completely free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he answered, drawing a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd think so?\u201d\"}"
