          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"85f3c05058f9fd50046f98bd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Sydney Carton halted in the street, uncertain where he should go. \u201cAt Tellson\u2019s banking-house at nine,\u201d he said, thoughtfully. \u201cWould it be wise, meanwhile, to let myself be seen? I believe so. These people had better know that such a man as I is here; it is a prudent safeguard, and may prove a needful preparation. But caution, caution, caution! Let me reason it through!\u201d\\n\\nArresting steps that had begun to lead him towards a purpose, he paced once or twice in the gathering darkness of the street, following the thought in his mind to all its possible results. His first conclusion was strengthened. \u201cIt is best,\u201d he said, at last determined, \u201cthat these people should know that such a man as I is here.\u201d Then he set his face towards Saint Antoine.\\n\\nDefarge had called himself, that day, the proprietor of a wine-shop in the suburb of Saint Antoine. For one who knew the city well, it was easy enough to discover his house without inquiry. When he had learned where it stood, Carton returned from those narrow streets, dined at a house of refreshment, and after dinner fell into a deep sleep. For the first time in many years, he drank no strong liquor. Since the previous night he had taken only a little weak, light wine; and on the previous night he had let the brandy trickle slowly down upon Mr. Lorry\u2019s hearth, like a man finished with it.\\n\\nIt was as late as seven when he woke, refreshed, and went again into the streets. Passing towards Saint Antoine, he paused before a shop-window containing a mirror, and made a slight change in the careless disposition of his loose cravat, coat-collar, and wild hair. Having done so, he went straight on to Defarge\u2019s and entered.\\n\\nBy chance, the only customer in the shop was Jacques Three, with his restless fingers and croaking voice. This man, whom Carton had seen on the Jury, stood drinking at the small counter and talking with the Defarges, husband and wife. The Vengeance joined in the talk, as though she were an established member of the household.\\n\\nWhen Carton came in, seated himself, and asked, in very poor French, for a small quantity of wine, Madame Defarge gave him a careless look, then a sharper one, and sharper still; then she came to him herself and asked what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated his former request.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d Madame Defarge asked, lifting her dark eyebrows with curiosity.\\n\\nAfter regarding her as though even one French word came slowly to his tongue, he replied in the same pronounced foreign accent.\"}"
