back to judge the effect\u2014put in a touch here and there\u2014judged it once more\u2014while Ben watched each motion, growing steadily more interested and absorbed. At last he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let _me_ whitewash some.\u201d\\n\\nTom reflected, and was nearly ready to agree; then he changed his mind:\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I\u2019m afraid it wouldn\u2019t quite do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly is mighty particular about this fence\u2014here on the street, you know\u2014but if it were the back fence, I wouldn\u2019t care and _she_ wouldn\u2019t either. Yes, she\u2019s mighty particular about this fence; it has to be done very carefully. I reckon there isn\u2019t one boy in a thousand\u2014maybe two thousand\u2014who can do it the way it needs to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that the truth? Oh, come now\u2014just let me try. Only a little\u2014I\u2019d let _you_ do it, if you were me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honest injun; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t allow him; Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t allow Sid.\u201d\"}"
