          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4411b7693da3e3ba13d9098c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Well, I says, I wanted the watermelon. But he said I didn\u2019t need it for getting out of prison; that was the difference. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to conceal a knife in, and smuggle it to Jim so he could kill the seneskal with it, that would have been all right. So I dropped it there, though I couldn\u2019t see what good there was in pretending to be a prisoner if I had to sit and chew over such gold-leaf distinctions every time I got a chance to steal a watermelon.\\n\\nWell, as I was telling you, we waited that morning until everybody had got settled to work, and there wasn\u2019t anybody to be seen about the yard; then Tom took the sack into the lean-to while I stood some distance off and kept watch. After a while he came out, and we went and sat on the woodpile to talk. He says:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s fixed now but the tools; and that\u2019s easy enough to arrange.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I says.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, for digging. We ain\u2019t going to _gnaw_ him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAin\u2019t those old broken-down picks and things in there good enough to dig a nigger out with?\u201d I says.\\n\\nHe faced round on me with such a pitying look it was enough to make anybody cry, and says:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, did you _ever_ hear of a prisoner having picks and shovels, with all the modern conveniences in his wardrobe, to dig himself out with? Now I ask you\u2014if there\u2019s any reasonableness in you\u2014what sort of chance would _that_ give him to be a hero? Why, they might just lend him the key and have done with it. Picks and shovels\u2014why, they wouldn\u2019t supply them to a king.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, then,\u201d I says, \u201cif we don\u2019t want picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA pair of case-knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig the foundations out from under that cabin with?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cConfound it, Tom, it\u2019s foolish.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt makes no difference how foolish it is; it\u2019s the _right_ way\u2014and the regular way. And there ain\u2019t any _other_ way that ever _I_ heard of, and I\u2019ve read every book that gives information on such matters. They always dig out with a case-knife\u2014and not through dirt, either; generally it\u2019s through solid rock. And it takes weeks and weeks and weeks, and forever and ever. Why, look at that prisoner in the bottom dungeon of the Castle Deef, in Marseilles harbor, that dug himself out that way; how long do you reckon _he_ was at it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, take a guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. A month and a half.\u201d\"}"
