          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ea0de4f420622e16a35001c4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Smallpox!\\n\\nI hurried to the king and spoke into his ear:\\n\\n\u201cOut the door at once, sire! The woman is dying of the same disease that ravaged the outskirts of Camelot two years past.\u201d\\n\\nHe did not stir.\\n\\n\u201cTruly, I shall stay\u2014and help besides.\u201d\\n\\nI whispered once more:\\n\\n\u201cKing, it cannot be. You must leave.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYe mean kindly, and ye speak with wisdom. Yet it were disgraceful for a king to show fear, and disgraceful for a belted knight to hold back his hand where there are those needing aid. Peace, I will not leave. It is you who must go. The Church\u2019s ban lies not upon me, but it forbids your presence here, and she will deal heavily with you if word reaches her of your offense.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a dreadful situation for him, and might well cost him his life, but there was no use arguing. If he thought his knightly honor involved, all debate was ended; he would remain, and nothing could stop him. I knew that. So I let the matter fall. The woman said:\\n\\n\u201cGood sir, in your mercy will ye climb that ladder and bring me word of what ye discover? Fear not to tell me, for there are times when even a mother\u2019s heart can break no further\u2014having been broken already.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWait,\u201d said the king, \u201cand give the woman food. I will go.\u201d He set down the knapsack.\\n\\nI turned to begin, but the king was already moving. He stopped and looked down at a man lying in the faint light, who had neither noticed us nor spoken until then.\\n\\n\u201cIs that your husband?\u201d asked the king.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDoes he sleep?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod be praised for that single mercy, yes\u2014these three hours. How shall I ever repay, in full, my gratitude? My heart is bursting with it for the sleep he sleeps now.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cWe shall be cautious. We will not wake him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, no, ye will not, for he is dead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDead?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; what a triumph it is to know it! No one can hurt him now, no one insult him further. He is in heaven and happy; or, if not there, he waits in hell and is content, for there he will find neither abbot nor bishop. We were children together; we were husband and wife these five-and-twenty years, never parted until this day. Think how long that is, to love and suffer side by side. This morning he was out of his senses, and in his fancy we were children again, roaming the happy fields; and in that innocent, joyful talk he wandered farther and farther, still gossiping lightly, and passed into those other fields we know nothing of, and was closed away from mortal sight.\"}"
