          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c2ad8f9436df4427f0a9691b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u2018If, however, you want one for use at home, I can provide you with an excellent item, and guarantee you will be satisfied with the result. May I ask who it is intended for? If it is for the police, or anyone connected with Scotland Yard, I am afraid I can do nothing for you. English detectives are truly our best friends, and I have always found that, by depending on their stupidity, we can do exactly as we please. I could not spare one of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I assure you,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, \u2018it has nothing whatever to do with the police. In fact, the clock is intended for the Dean of Chichester.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear me! I had no idea you felt so strongly about religion, Lord Arthur. Few young men do these days.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am afraid you give me too much credit, Herr Winckelkopf,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, blushing. \u2018The truth is, I know absolutely nothing about theology.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Then it is a purely private matter?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Entirely private.\u2019\\n\\nHerr Winckelkopf shrugged and left the room. A few minutes later he returned carrying a round cake of dynamite the size of a penny, along with a charming little French clock topped by an ormolu figure of Liberty trampling the hydra of Despotism.\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s face lit up at the sight of it. \u2018That is exactly what I want,\u2019 he cried. \u2018Now tell me how it is set off.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ah, that is my secret,\u2019 Herr Winckelkopf replied, studying his invention with a well-earned expression of pride. \u2018Tell me when you want it to explode, and I will set the mechanism for that moment.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, today is Tuesday, and if you could send it out at once\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018That is impossible. I have a great deal of important work in hand for some friends in Moscow. Still, I could send it tomorrow.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, that will be quite soon enough!\u2019 said Lord Arthur politely. \u2018If it is delivered tomorrow night or Thursday morning. As for the moment of the explosion, let it be Friday at exactly noon. The Dean is always at home then.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Friday at noon,\u2019 repeated Herr Winckelkopf, making a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau near the fireplace.\\n\\n\u2018And now,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, getting to his feet, \u2018please tell me how much I owe you.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018It is such a small matter, Lord Arthur, that I do not wish to charge you. The dynamite costs seven shillings and sixpence, the clock three pounds ten, and the carriage about five shillings. I am only too happy to oblige any friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018But your trouble, Herr Winckelkopf?\u2019\"}"
