          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"11a0c3ba2a1a36113c0e1eab\",\"rewritten_text\":\"According to recent reports from Rotterdam, that city seems to be in a state of intense philosophical excitement. Events have occurred there so unexpected, so new, and so contrary to accepted ideas that I have no doubt all Europe is by now in an uproar, physics in confusion, and reason and astronomy at war with each other.\\n\\nIt seems that on the \u2014\u2014 day of \u2014\u2014 (I am not certain of the date), a huge crowd had gathered in the great Exchange square of the orderly city of Rotterdam, for reasons not clearly stated. The day was warm\u2014unusually warm for the season\u2014and scarcely a breath of wind was moving. The crowd was not displeased when brief, friendly showers now and then fell from the great white clouds that drifted unevenly across the blue sky. Yet around noon, a small but striking stir appeared among the people. Ten thousand tongues began clattering; then, in the next instant, ten thousand faces turned upward, ten thousand pipes dropped at once from the corners of ten thousand mouths, and a cry, like nothing but the roar of Niagara, rang long, loud, and fiercely through the whole area around Rotterdam.\\n\\nThe cause of this uproar soon became clear enough. From behind the enormous mass of one of the sharply outlined clouds already mentioned, something strange, mixed in form, and apparently solid slowly emerged into an open patch of blue sky. It was so oddly shaped and so whimsically constructed that the sturdy burghers standing below, mouths open, could neither understand it nor admire it enough. What could it be? In the name of all the vrows and devils in Rotterdam, what could it possibly mean? No one knew or could guess. No one\u2014not even the burgomaster, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk\u2014had the slightest clue to solve the mystery. Since nothing more sensible could be done, every man carefully put his pipe back into the corner of his mouth, raised his right eye toward the sight, puffed, paused, waddled about, and grunted meaningfully\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and finally puffed again.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the object of such curiosity, and the cause of so much smoke, came lower and lower toward the worthy city. Within a few minutes it was close enough to be clearly seen. It appeared to be\u2014yes! it was certainly a kind of balloon; but surely Rotterdam had never seen a balloon like it before.\"}"
