th his left hand, stood looking down into her face as she looked up into his. With his right hand, he alternately rubbed his chin, tugged his wig by the ears, or gestured to emphasize his words.\\n\\n\u201cMiss Manette, it was I. And you will see how truthfully I described myself just now, when I said I had no feelings and that every connection I have with my fellow human beings is merely business, if you consider that I have never seen you since. No; you have been a ward of Tellson\u2019s House ever since, and I have been occupied ever since with Tellson\u2019s House\u2019s other business. Feelings! I have neither time nor opportunity for them. I spend my entire life, miss, turning an enormous financial mangle.\u201d\"}"
