          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8ecf73ef3168648ffe8979a3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The surrounding oaks sheltered a tribe of nightingales\u2014there am I now; Idris, in the lovely spring of youth, stands beside me\u2014remember, I am but twenty-two, and scarcely seventeen summers have passed above the beloved of my heart. The river, swelled by autumn rains, had overflowed the low grounds, and Adrian, in his favourite boat, was engaged in the perilous sport of gathering the highest branch from a drowned oak. Art thou weary of life, Adrian, that thou dost thus trifle with danger?\u2014\\n\\nHe had won his prize, and guided his boat through the inundation; we watched him with fearful eyes, but the current bore him away from us. He was obliged to land much farther below, and make a wide circuit before he could rejoin us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris, as he sprang ashore and waved the bough above his head in sign of triumph; \u201cwe will await him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe were left alone; the sun had gone down; the nightingales commenced their song; the evening star shone clear amid the tide of radiance still lingering, though fading, in the west. The blue eyes of my angelic girl rested on that dear image of herself: \u201cHow that light throbs,\u201d she said, \u201cwhich is the life of the star. Its wavering brightness appears to tell that its condition, like ours on earth, is uncertain and changeful; it fears, I think, and loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLook not upon the star, dear and generous friend,\u201d I cried, \u201cnor read love in its quivering beams; turn not to remote worlds; speak not of a sentiment that is only imagined. Long have I been mute; long, even unto sickness, have I yearned to speak with you, and yield my soul, my life, my whole being to you. Look not on the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that everlasting spark intercede for me; let it stand as witness and advocate, silent in its shining\u2014love is to me what light is to the star; while that remains unextinguished by annihilation, so long will I love you.\u201d\\n\\nFor ever hidden from the world\u2019s unfeeling eye must remain the rapture of that instant. Even now I feel her graceful form pressed against my overcharged heart\u2014even now sight, pulse, and breath grow faint and fail at memory of that first kiss. Slowly and without speech we went to meet Adrian, whom we heard drawing near.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to come back to me after he had escorted his sister home. That same evening, as we walked the moonlit paths of the forest, I poured out to my friend my entire heart, its rapture and its hope. For a moment he seemed troubled\u2014\u201cI might have anticipated this,\u201d he said, \u201cwhat contention will follow now!\u201d\"}"
