o arrange my thoughts in proper order for my attempt. My heart beat quickly as I forced myself to speak to him, for I was determined not to be turned away; yet I trembled to imagine what effect my words might have upon him. At last, after much hesitation, I began:\\n\\n\u201cYour kindness to me, my dearest father, and the affection\u2014the excessive affection\u2014you showed me when you first returned will, I hope, excuse me in your eyes for daring to speak to you, though with a daughter\u2019s tender love, also with the freedom of a friend and an equal.\u201d\"}"
