r lightning is waiting, ready like a charge in a gun, but it costs you nothing until you fire it. Oh, yes, the one ground connection--\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly! I cannot think how I missed that. It is not merely cheaper, but more effective than the other arrangement, because if wires snap or become entangled, no damage results.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, particularly if we have a tell-tale in the cave and cut off the broken wire. Well, continue. The gatlings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes--that is settled. At the center of the innermost circle, upon a broad platform six feet high, I have placed a battery of thirteen gatling guns, with an ample supply of ammunition.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is right. They cover every approach, and when the Church's knights come, there will be music. The edge of the precipice above the cave--\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have a wire fence there, and a gatling.\u201d\"}"
