          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cd00bcc0051ed7f8f851f87e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, everybody lives that way, Huck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, that doesn\u2019t make any difference. I\u2019m not everybody, and I can\u2019t stand it. It\u2019s awful, being tied down like that. And food comes too easy\u2014I don\u2019t take any interest in eating when it\u2019s that way. I have to ask to go fishing; I have to ask to go swimming\u2014damned if I don\u2019t have to ask to do everything. And I had to talk so proper it wasn\u2019t any comfort\u2014I had to go up in the attic and let loose for a while every day, just to get the taste back in my mouth, or I\u2019d have died, Tom. The widow wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me yell, or gape, or stretch, or scratch myself in front of people\u2014\u201d Then, with a sudden burst of particular irritation and hurt: \u201cAnd damn it, she prayed all the time! I never saw such a woman! I had to get away, Tom\u2014I just had to. Besides, school is going to open, and I\u2019d have had to go\u2014well, I wouldn\u2019t stand that, Tom. Look here, Tom, being rich isn\u2019t what it\u2019s made out to be. It\u2019s nothing but worry and worry, sweat and sweat, and wishing you were dead all the time. These clothes suit me, and this barrel suits me, and I\u2019m never going to give them up again. Tom, I never would have gotten into all this trouble if it hadn\u2019t been for that money; now you take my share along with yours, and give me a dime now and then\u2014not too often, because I don\u2019t care a damn for anything unless it\u2019s fairly hard to get\u2014and you go ask the widow to excuse me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. It wouldn\u2019t be fair; and besides, if you try this life a little longer, you\u2019ll come to like it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLike it! Sure\u2014the way I\u2019d like a hot stove if I sat on it long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich, and I won\u2019t live in those cursed, smothering houses. I like the woods, and the river, and hogsheads, and I\u2019ll stick to them, too. Damn it all! Just when we\u2019d gotten guns, and a cave, and everything fixed to start robbing, this damned foolishness has to come up and spoil it all!\u201d\\n\\nTom saw his chance\u2014\\n\\n\u201cLook here, Huck, being rich isn\u2019t going to stop me from becoming a robber.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo! Oh, that\u2019s great; do you really mean it, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI mean it as surely as I\u2019m sitting here. But, Huck, we can\u2019t let you into the gang if you aren\u2019t respectable, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHuck\u2019s joy went out.\\n\\n\u201cCan\u2019t let me in, Tom?\u201d\"}"
