ile shaking his head, \u201cif you can imagine this little place under siege, it could hold out a devilishly long time for provisions.\u201d\\n\\nThen he led me to a bower about twelve yards away, though the path wound about so cleverly that it took a long time to reach it. In this retreat, our glasses had already been set out. Our punch was cooling in an ornamental lake beside which the bower stood. The water, circular in shape, had an island in the middle that might have supplied the salad for supper; and Wemmick had made a fountain in it which, when you started a little mill and pulled a cork from a pipe, sprayed so strongly that it made the back of your hand quite wet.\"}"
