ve me formally bound as Joe\u2019s apprentice in the presence of the magistrates. I say we went, but Pumblechook pushed me along, exactly as though I had just picked a pocket or set fire to a haystack. Indeed, the general impression in court was that I had been caught red-handed; for as Pumblechook shoved me ahead of him through the crowd, I heard some people ask, \u201cWhat\u2019s he done?\u201d and others say, \u201cHe\u2019s only a young one, but he looks bad, doesn\u2019t he?\u201d One mild-looking, kindly person even handed me a tract decorated with a woodcut of a wicked young man wearing enough chains for a whole sausage shop, titled TO BE READ IN MY CELL.\\n\\nThe Hall seemed a strange place to me, with pews higher than those in a church, people leaning over them to watch, and imposing Justices\u2014one wearing a powdered wig\u2014reclining in chairs with folded arms, taking snuff, dozing, writing, or reading newspapers. There were also some glossy black portraits on the walls, which my untrained eye took for a mixture of hard candy and sticking plaster.\"}"
