          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7d79b46b0914fd51d5e2936e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Dearest Rose, just one more!\u201d cried Harry, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world would call it\u2014if I had been meant for some quiet, unknown life\u2014if I had been poor, ill, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or has the chance that I may rise to wealth and honour created this doubt?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d said Rose. \u201cThe question does not exist, and never will. It is unfair, almost cruel, to ask it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I hardly dare hope,\u201d Harry replied, \u201cit will bring a ray of happiness to my lonely road and light the way ahead. It is no small thing to give so much, with only a few short words, to someone who loves you above everything else. Oh, Rose, in the name of my deep and lasting love; in the name of all I have suffered for you, and all you condemn me to suffer; answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your life had been different,\u201d Rose answered, \u201cif you had been only a little, but not so greatly, above me; if I could have helped and comforted you in some humble, peaceful life away from the world, instead of being a stain and burden among ambitious and distinguished people; I would have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now; but then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs Rose made this confession, memories of old hopes she had treasured as a girl long ago crowded into her mind. They brought tears, as old hopes do when they return faded and dead; yet they gave her relief.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot help this weakness, and it only makes my resolve stronger,\u201d said Rose, holding out her hand. \u201cI truly must leave you now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask for one promise,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014within a year, perhaps much sooner\u2014I may speak to you again on this subject, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to urge me to change my proper decision,\u201d Rose replied with a sad smile. \u201cThat would be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnly to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it finally. I will place at your feet whatever rank or fortune I may have; and if you still keep to your present decision, I will not try, by word or action, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cIt is only one more pain, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand again.\"}"
