h he were on fire. Then, confused and frightened, he turned and ran. Not knowing what he was doing, he fled as fast as his feet could carry him.\\n\\nAll this happened within a minute. At the very moment Oliver began to run, the old gentleman put his hand into his pocket and found his handkerchief missing. He turned sharply around. Seeing the boy speeding away so quickly, he naturally decided that Oliver was the thief. Shouting, \u201cStop thief!\u201d at the top of his voice, he ran after him, still holding the book in his hand.\"}"
