in the character and manners of the family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank you, dear Miss Woodhouse. Yes, indeed, every thing in the world is there to make her happy. Excepting the Sucklings and the Bragges, there is no other nursery establishment so liberal and elegant in all Mrs. Elton\u2019s acquaintance. Mrs. Smallridge, a most charming woman!\u2014A manner of living nearly equal to Maple Grove\u2014and as for the children, except the little Sucklings and little Bragges, there are no such elegant, sweet children anywhere. Jane will be received with such consideration and kindness!\u2014It will be all pleasure, a life entirely of pleasure.\u2014And her salary!\u2014I truly cannot presume to mention her salary to you, Miss Woodhouse.\"}"
