he scythe. At his master\u2019s direction, Jupiter began cutting a path for us to the base of an enormously tall tulip tree. It stood on the level ground among eight or ten oaks and surpassed them all\u2014and every other tree I had ever seen\u2014in the beauty of its foliage and shape, the broad spread of its branches, and the overall majesty of its appearance.\"}"
