ate; but the word republic had become stale to common ears, and many\u2014whether a majority, events would show\u2014longed for the glitter and display of royalty. Ryland was stirred to resistance; he declared that only his tolerance had allowed this party to grow, but the time for indulgence had passed, and with one sweep of his arm he would clear away the cobwebs that blinded his countrymen.\\n\\nWhen Raymond entered the coffee-room, his friends greeted him almost with a shout. They crowded around him, counted their numbers, and explained why they were now to gain the support of certain members who had not yet declared themselves.\"}"
