          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4e4c49ed93941b8bdcaef3c5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, Jup,\u201d I said, \u201cwhat is wrong now? How is your master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, to tell de truth, massa, he ain\u2019t as well as he might be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot well! I am truly sorry to hear it. What does he complain of?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDat\u2019s just it! He never complains of nothin\u2019\u2014but he\u2019s mighty sick all de same.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery sick, Jupiter! Why didn\u2019t you say so immediately? Is he confined to bed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, he ain\u2019t! He ain\u2019t confined nowhere\u2014that\u2019s where de trouble lies\u2014my mind\u2019s been mighty heavy about poor Massa Will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJupiter, I would like to understand what you mean. You say your master is ill. Has he not told you what is wrong with him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, massa, it ain\u2019t worth getting angry over\u2014Massa Will says there\u2019s nothin\u2019 at all wrong with him\u2014but what makes him walk around looking like this, with his head down and his shoulders hunched, white as a goose? And then he keeps a cipher all de time\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a what, Jupiter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a cipher with figures on a slate\u2014the strangest figures I ever did see. I\u2019m beginning to get scared, I tell you. I have to keep a mighty close eye on him noovers. The other day he slipped away before sunrise and was gone the whole blessed day. I had a big stick cut and ready to give him a devilish good beating when he came back\u2014but I\u2019m such a fool I hadn\u2019t the heart after all\u2014he looked so very poorly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEh? What? Ah, yes! On the whole, I think you had better not be too hard on the poor fellow\u2014don\u2019t flog him, Jupiter\u2014he can scarcely bear it. But can you form no idea what has caused this illness, or rather this change in his behavior? Has anything unpleasant happened since I saw you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, massa, there ain\u2019t been nothin\u2019 unpleasant since then\u2014it was before then I\u2019m afraid\u2014it was the very day you were there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow? What do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, massa, I mean de bug\u2014there now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDe bug. I\u2019m mighty certain Massa Will was bit somewhere about de head by that gold bug.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd what reason have you, Jupiter, for such a belief?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cClaws enough, massa, and a mouth too. I never saw such a devilish bug\u2014he kicks and bites everything that comes near him. Massa Will caught him first, but had to let him go again mighty quick, I tell you\u2014then was when he must have got bit. I didn\u2019t like the look of de bug\u2019s mouth myself, nohow, so I wouldn\u2019t take hold of him with my fingers, but caught him with a piece of paper I found.\u201d\"}"
