s and invitations, were planning a match between the heir and the young lady. Such a match could never have suited his ideas of wealth and independence. That was why he drew back, I assure you. He told me the whole story. He hid nothing from me. It was strange that, after I had just left you behind in Bath, my first and closest acquaintance after my marriage should be your cousin, and that through him I should keep hearing of your father and sister.\u201d\"}"
