as very glad of it, though everyone else was miserable\u2014which was only natural. I said:\\n\\n\u201cThe king, by his silence, still agrees to the terms.\u201d Then I raised my hands\u2014held them that way for a moment\u2014and said, with the most dreadful solemnity, \u201cLet the enchantment dissolve and pass away harmlessly!\u201d\\n\\nFor a moment there was no answer in that profound darkness and graveyard silence. But when the silver edge of the sun appeared a moment or two later, the assembly burst into a mighty shout and surged down like a flood to overwhelm me with blessings and gratitude; and Clarence was certainly not the last in that wave.\"}"
