          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8d60889197c330a04ab8a1a1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The surrounding oaks were home to a colony of nightingales\u2014there I am now; Idris, in the lovely bloom of youth, is beside me\u2014remember, I am only twenty-two, and scarcely seventeen summers have passed over the beloved of my heart. The river, swollen by autumn rains, had flooded the lowlands, and Adrian, in his favourite boat, was engaged in the dangerous amusement of plucking the highest branch from a submerged oak. Are you tired of life, Adrian, that you play so recklessly with danger?\u2014\\n\\nHe had won his prize and steered his boat through the flood; we watched him anxiously, but the current swept him away from us. He was forced to land much farther downstream and take a long circuit before he could rejoin us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris, as he sprang ashore and waved the branch above his head in triumph; \u201cwe will wait for him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe were alone together; the sun had set; the nightingales began to sing; the evening star shone clearly amid the light that still lingered in the west. The blue eyes of my angelic girl rested on that sweet image of herself. \u201cHow its light trembles,\u201d she said, \u201cthat is the life of the star. Its wavering brightness seems to say that its condition, like ours on earth, is uncertain and changeable; I think it fears, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not gaze at the star, dear, generous friend,\u201d I cried. \u201cDo not read love in its trembling rays; do not look toward distant worlds or speak of a feeling that is only imagined. I have been silent for so long; so long have I longed, even to illness, to speak to you and lay my soul, my life, my whole being before you. Do not look at the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that eternal spark plead for me; let it be my witness and advocate, silent as it shines\u2014love is to me what light is to the star; as long as it remains uneclipsed by annihilation, so long will I love you.\u201d\\n\\nForever hidden from the world\u2019s cold eye must remain the rapture of that moment. Even now I feel her graceful form pressed against my overflowing heart\u2014even now sight, pulse, and breath grow faint and fail at the memory of that first kiss. Slowly and silently, we went to meet Adrian, whom we heard drawing near.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to return to me after he had taken his sister home. That same evening, as we walked along the moonlit paths of the forest, I poured out my whole heart\u2014its joy and its hope\u2014to my friend. For a moment he seemed troubled. \u201cI might have foreseen this,\u201d he said. \u201cWhat conflict will follow now!\u201d\"}"
