gnaud. Madame L\u2019Espanaye possessed some property. She had opened an account at his bank in the spring of that year\u2014eight years earlier. She made frequent small deposits. She had withdrawn nothing until three days before her death, when she personally took out 4,000 francs. The money was paid in gold, and a clerk accompanied her home with it.\\n\\n\u201c_Adolphe Le Bon_, clerk at Mignaud et Fils, states that on the day in question, around noon, he accompanied Madame L\u2019Espanaye to her home with the 4,000 francs, packed in two bags. When the door was opened, Mademoiselle L. appeared and took one bag from his hands, while the old lady took the other.\u201d\"}"
