          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0a0214fcdd9f021df4d58793\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cThese thoughts soothed me, and that afternoon I fell into a deep sleep; but the fever in my blood would not permit peaceful dreams. The terrible scene of the day before played endlessly before my eyes: the women fleeing, and the furious Felix dragging me away from his father\u2019s feet. I woke exhausted, and, finding that night had already fallen, crept from my hiding place to search for food.\\n\\n\u201cWhen I had satisfied my hunger, I made my way along the familiar path leading to the cottage. Everything there was quiet. I slipped into my hovel and waited silently for the usual hour when the family rose. That hour passed; the sun climbed high in the sky, yet the cottagers did not appear. I shook violently, fearing some dreadful disaster. The cottage was dark within, and I heard no movement; I cannot describe the torment of that suspense.\\n\\n\u201cSoon two countrymen passed by, but they stopped near the cottage and began talking with violent gestures. I could not understand them, for they spoke the language of the country, which differed from that of my protectors. Shortly afterward, however, Felix came toward them with another man. I was astonished, since I knew he had not left the cottage that morning, and I listened anxiously, hoping his words would explain these strange events.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Have you considered,\u2019 his companion said to him, \u2018that you will have to pay three months\u2019 rent and lose the produce of your garden? I do not wish to take unfair advantage of you, and so I ask that you take a few days to consider your decision.\u2019\\n\\n\u201c\u2018It is completely useless,\u2019 Felix replied. \u2018We can never live in your cottage again. My father\u2019s life is in the greatest danger because of the dreadful event I have told you about. My wife and sister will never recover from their horror. I beg you, do not argue with me any longer. Take possession of your house, and let me flee this place.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cFelix trembled violently as he spoke. He and his companion entered the cottage, remained there a few minutes, and then left. I never saw any member of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\n\u201cFor the rest of the day, I remained in my hovel in a state of blank, senseless despair. My protectors had gone, breaking the only bond that connected me to the world. For the first time, revenge and hatred filled my heart, and I made no effort to restrain them. Letting myself be carried along by that current, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\u201d\"}"
