          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"57095982f5253f8f41bea9a2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But in that bitter attack on Chantilly, published in yesterday\u2019s \u2018Mus\u00e9e,\u2019 the satirist made some shameful references to the cobbler\u2019s change of name when he became an actor, and quoted a Latin line we had often discussed. I mean the line\\n\\nPerdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\\n\\n\u201cI had told you that it referred to Orion, once spelled Urion; and because of certain pointed details connected with that explanation, I knew you could not have forgotten it. It was clear, then, that you would connect the two ideas of Orion and Chantilly. I saw that you had done so by the kind of smile that crossed your lips. You thought of the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Until then, you had been walking with a stoop; but now I saw you straighten yourself to your full height. I was then certain that you were thinking of Chantilly\u2019s small size. At that moment I broke into your thoughts by saying that, since Chantilly was in fact such a little fellow, he would be better suited to the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s.\u201d\\n\\nNot long afterward, we were reading an evening edition of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux\u201d when the following paragraphs caught our attention.\\n\\n\u201cExtraordinary Murders.\u2014This morning, at about three o\u2019clock, the residents of the Quartier St. Roch were awakened by a series of terrible screams, apparently coming from the fourth floor of a house in the Rue Morgue. The house was known to be occupied only by Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After some delay, caused by an unsuccessful attempt to gain entry in the usual way, the gate was forced open with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors entered with two gendarmes. By then the cries had stopped; but as the group rushed up the first flight of stairs, they heard two or more harsh voices arguing angrily, apparently from the upper part of the house. When they reached the second landing, these sounds had also stopped, and all was completely quiet. The group separated and hurried from room to room. On reaching a large rear chamber on the fourth floor\u2014the door was locked, with the key inside, and had to be forced open\u2014they found a sight that filled everyone present with both horror and astonishment.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in complete disorder. Furniture had been broken and scattered in every direction. There was only one bedstead, and its bed had been removed and thrown into the middle of the floor. On a chair lay a razor, smeared with blood.\"}"
