          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"155e3b4f059dc62bee714a16\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the sight of these things, Jupiter could hardly contain his joy, but his master\u2019s face showed deep disappointment. Still, he urged us to keep working, and scarcely had he spoken when I stumbled and fell forward, catching the toe of my boot in a large iron ring half buried in the loose soil.\\n\\nWe now set to work seriously, and I have never spent ten minutes in greater excitement. In that time, we completely uncovered a long wooden chest. Its perfect condition and remarkable hardness showed that it had been treated with some preserving mineral process\u2014perhaps bichloride of mercury. The box was three and a half feet long, three feet wide, and two and a half feet deep. It was tightly bound with riveted wrought-iron bands that formed an open lattice over its entire surface. Near the top of each side were three iron rings\u2014six altogether\u2014so that six people could get a firm grip on it. Even our combined strength could move the chest only slightly in its resting place. We immediately saw that it was impossible to lift such a weight. Fortunately, the lid was held shut only by two sliding bolts. We pulled them back, trembling and breathless with anxiety. In an instant, a treasure beyond calculation lay shining before us. When the lantern light reached into the pit, a blaze of light flashed upward from the mixed heap of gold and jewels, dazzling our eyes.\\n\\nI will not try to describe what I felt as I looked at it. Amazement, of course, was strongest. Legrand seemed worn out by excitement and said very little. For several minutes, Jupiter\u2019s face was as pale as it could possibly become. He seemed stunned, as if struck by lightning. Soon he dropped to his knees in the pit and plunged his bare arms up to the elbows in the gold, leaving them there as though enjoying a bath. At last, with a deep sigh, he cried out as if speaking to himself:\\n\\n\u201cAnd dis all cum ob de goole-bug! de putty goole-bug! de poor little goole-bug, what I boosed in dat sabage kind ob style! Aint you shamed ob yourself, nigger?\u2014answer me dat!\u201d\\n\\nAt last, I had to rouse both master and servant to the need to remove the treasure. It was getting late, and we had to work hard if we meant to get everything under cover before daylight. It was hard to decide what to do, and we spent much time discussing it, because all our thoughts were so confused.\"}"
