o make me associate these allusions with Provis. Naturally, I was quite certain, and secure in the certainty, that Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say I surprise you, Mr. Pip; indeed, I can see that I do. But it is exceedingly strange! You will scarcely credit what I am about to tell you. I could scarcely credit it myself, if it were told to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed?\u201d said I.\\n\\n\u201cNo, indeed. Mr. Pip, do you recall, in former days, a certain Christmas Day, when you were a mere child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it perfectly well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd do you remember there was a pursuit after two convicts, that we joined it, that Gargery carried you upon his back, that I led the way, and that you followed me as well as you were able?\u201d\"}"
