ent beyond the Straits, and I was never in the West Indies. We do not count Bermuda or the Bahamas, you know, as the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had not a word to offer in disagreement; throughout her life, she could not have accused herself of calling them anything at all.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft continued, \u201cnothing can surpass the comforts of a man-of-war; I mean, of the higher rates. On a frigate, naturally, one is more confined, though any sensible woman can be perfectly happy in one. And I can safely say that the happiest part of my life has been spent aboard a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\u201d\"}"
