ng-sheet as he raced down the corridor and finally dropped the rusty dagger into the Minister\u2019s jack-boots, where the butler found it the next morning. Once safely inside his own room, he threw himself onto a small pallet bed and hid his face beneath the covers. After a while, however, the brave old Canterville spirit returned, and he resolved to go and speak to the other ghost as soon as daylight came. So, just as dawn touched the hills with silver, he went back toward the place where he had first seen the grim phantom, thinking that two ghosts were, after all, better than one, and that with his new friend\u2019s help he might safely take on the twins.\"}"
