{"request_id":"3c490fe1edcbd18f0f9f28e6","rewritten_text":"Indeed, I had no concern for her. She was what people call a capable woman, fully able to manage worldly affairs without my help. To tell the truth, I believe she had always regarded me as an idle boy, a mere burden, fit for nothing but building castles in the air, and was rather pleased to be rid of me. It was a dark night when I said good-bye to her, and, taking with me as aides-de-camp the three creditors who had caused me so much trouble, we carried the balloon, with its car and equipment, by a circuitous route to the station where the other articles had been stored. There we found everything untouched, and I set to work at once.

“It was the first of April. The night, as I have said, was dark; not a star was visible; and a drizzling rain, falling now and then, made us thoroughly uncomfortable. But my chief concern was for the balloon, which, despite the varnish protecting it, was beginning to grow rather heavy with damp; the powder, too, was liable to be spoiled. I therefore kept my three duns hard at work, packing ice around the central cask and stirring the acid in the others. Yet they would not stop pestering me with questions about what I meant to do with all this apparatus, and they complained bitterly of the dreadful labor I made them endure. They could not see, they said, what benefit could come from being soaked to the skin merely to take part in such horrible incantations. I began to feel uneasy and worked with all my strength, for I truly believe the fools thought I had made a bargain with the devil, and that what I was doing was, in short, no better than it ought to be. I was therefore greatly afraid they would abandon me altogether. Still, I managed to calm them by promising to pay every debt in full as soon as I had brought the present undertaking to an end. Naturally, they put their own interpretation on these assurances, imagining, no doubt, that I would somehow come into possession of vast sums of ready money; and so long as I paid all I owed them, with a little extra for their services, I dare say they cared very little what became of either my soul or my body.

“In about four and a half hours, I found the balloon sufficiently inflated. I then attached the car and placed all my instruments inside—not forgetting the condensing apparatus, an ample supply of water, and a large store of provisions, such as pemmican, which contains much nourishment in comparatively little space."}

