ip\u2019s residence, only by a lane.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think you said she was a widow, sir? Does she have any family?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe has only one daughter, the heiress of Rosings and of a very large fortune.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d cried Mrs. Bennet, shaking her head, \u201cthen she is better provided for than many girls. And what sort of young lady is she? Is she pretty?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe is a most charming young lady indeed. Lady Catherine herself says that, in terms of true beauty, Miss de Bourgh is far superior to the prettiest women of her sex, because there is something in her features that marks her as a young woman of distinguished birth.\u201d\"}"
