ten such a secret. As it was, I assumed the cryptograph was English.\\n\\n\u201cYou see that there are no spaces between the words. If there had been, the task would have been fairly easy. In that case, I would have begun by comparing and analyzing the shorter words; and if a one-letter word had appeared, as was most likely\u2014an a or an I, for example\u2014I would have considered the solution certain. But since there were no divisions, my first step was to find the most common letters, as well as the rarest.\u201d\"}"
