          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d0d612c9cdf3fab81b4fb827\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Yet in that acrid _tirade_ against Chantilly, published in yesterday\u2019s \u2018_Mus\u00e9e_,\u2019 the satirist, indulging in certain shameful allusions to the cobbler\u2019s alteration of name when he assumed the buskin, cited a Latin verse of which we have frequently spoken. I refer to the line\\n\\nPerdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\\n\\n\u201cI had informed you that it referred to Orion, once spelled Urion; and, owing to certain pointed associations attached to this explanation, I knew you could not have forgotten it. It was evident, then, that you would be sure to connect the ideas of Orion and Chantilly. That you had done so I perceived from the nature of the smile that crossed your lips. You were thinking of the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Until then, you had walked with a stoop; but I now saw you straighten yourself to your full stature. I was certain, therefore, that you were considering Chantilly\u2019s small figure. At that moment I broke in upon your reflections by observing that, since he was in truth a very little fellow\u2014that Chantilly\u2014he would be better suited to the _Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s_.\u201d\\n\\nSoon afterward, we were examining an evening issue of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux,\u201d when the following account caught our notice.\\n\\n\u201c_Extraordinary Murders_.\u2014At about three o\u2019clock this morning, the residents of the Quartier St. Roch were awakened by a series of dreadful shrieks, apparently proceeding from the fourth floor of a house in the Rue Morgue, known to be occupied solely by a Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After some delay, caused by an unsuccessful effort to gain entrance in the ordinary way, the gateway was forced with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors entered, attended by two _gendarmes_. By then the cries had stopped; yet, as the party hurried up the first flight of stairs, two or more harsh voices, engaged in angry dispute, were heard, and appeared to come from the upper portion of the house. On reaching the second landing, these sounds too had ceased, and all was utterly still. The party separated and hastened from chamber to chamber. Reaching a large rear room on the fourth floor, (whose door, found locked with the key within, was broken open,) they beheld a scene that filled all present with as much amazement as horror.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in the utmost confusion\u2014the furniture shattered and scattered in every direction. There was but one bedstead; the bed had been taken from it and flung into the center of the floor. Upon a chair lay a razor, stained with blood.\"}"
