          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"be62fdfa22ff3bf1d9a4a2db\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Well, I said, I needed the watermelon. But he said I didn\u2019t need it for getting out of prison; that was the difference. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to hide a knife in and smuggle it to Jim so he could kill the seneschal, that would have been all right. So I left it at that, though I couldn\u2019t see the point of pretending to be a prisoner if I had to sit around chewing over a lot of hair-splitting distinctions every time I saw a chance to steal a watermelon.\\n\\nWell, as I was saying, we waited that morning until everybody had settled down to work and nobody was in sight around the yard. Then Tom carried the sack into the lean-to while I stood some distance off to keep watch. After a while he came out, and we went and sat on the woodpile to talk. He said:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s all right now except the tools, and that\u2019s easy enough to fix.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, for digging. We aren\u2019t going to gnaw him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAren\u2019t those old broken picks and things in there good enough to dig a nigger out with?\u201d I said.\\n\\nHe turned on me with such a pitying look it could have made a person cry, and said:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, did you ever hear of a prisoner having picks and shovels, and all the modern conveniences in his wardrobe to dig himself out with? Now I want to ask you\u2014if you have any sense at all\u2014what kind of a chance would that give him to be a hero? Why, they might as well lend him the key and be done with it. Picks and shovels\u2014they wouldn\u2019t provide those for a king.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell then,\u201d I said, \u201cif we don\u2019t want picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA couple of case-knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig the foundations out from under that cabin with?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cConfound it, Tom, that\u2019s foolish.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt doesn\u2019t matter how foolish it is; it\u2019s the right way, and it\u2019s the regular way. And there isn\u2019t any other way that I ever heard of, and I\u2019ve read all the books that give information about these things. They always dig out with a case-knife\u2014and not through dirt, either; generally it\u2019s through solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, forever and ever. Why, look at that prisoner in the bottom dungeon of the Castle Deef, in the harbor of Marseilles, who dug himself out that way. How long do you suppose he was at it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. A month and a half.\u201d\"}"
