          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"53e4b07be7749c2bdb5de370\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After I had sent them in, I could not stay away from the places where they were. I felt that they seemed more hopeful, less desperate, when I was near them. In this restless, painful state of mind, I would walk the streets in the evening, passing the offices and houses where I had left the petitions. Even now, the tired western streets of London on a cold, dusty spring night, with their rows of severe, closed-up houses and long lines of lamps, make me sad because of that memory.\\n\\nThe daily visits I was allowed to make to him were now shorter, and he was watched more closely. Believing, or imagining, that they suspected me of meaning to bring him poison, I asked to be searched before I sat beside his bed. I told the officer who was always present that I would do anything to convince him that my intentions were honest. No one was cruel to him or to me. A duty had to be done, and it was done, but not harshly. The officer always told me that he was worse; and some other sick prisoners in the room, along with prisoners who cared for them as nurses\u2014criminals, but not unable to be kind, thank God!\u2014always said the same.\\n\\nAs the days passed, I noticed more and more that he would lie quietly looking at the white ceiling, with no light in his face, until something I said brightened it for a moment. Then the light would fade again. Sometimes he was almost, or entirely, unable to speak. Then he answered me with slight pressures of my hand, and I came to understand his meaning very well.\\n\\nTen days had passed when I saw a greater change in him than I had seen before. His eyes were turned toward the door, and they brightened when I came in.\\n\\n\u201cDear boy,\u201d he said as I sat beside his bed, \u201cI thought you was late. But I knowed you couldn\u2019t be that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is exactly the time,\u201d I said. \u201cI waited for it at the gate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou always waits at the gate, don\u2019t you, dear boy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. So as not to lose a moment.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank\u2019ee, dear boy, thank\u2019ee. God bless you! You\u2019ve never deserted me, dear boy.\u201d\\n\\nI pressed his hand silently, because I could not forget that I had once intended to desert him.\\n\\n\u201cAnd best of all,\u201d he said, \u201cyou\u2019ve been more comfortable alonger me, since I was under a dark cloud, than when the sun shone.\u201d\"}"
