          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"82aa9270f41ef82bf293ec19\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d said Duff.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, rendering the word yokel for the ladies\u2019 benefit, I take your meaning to be that this effort was not made by a countryman?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s the thing, master,\u201d returned Blathers. \u201cThis is all concerning the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll,\u201d answered the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this here about the boy the servants are talking of?\u201d asked Blathers.\\n\\n\u201cNothing whatever,\u201d replied the doctor. \u201cOne of the alarmed servants has chosen to imagine that he had something to do with this attempt to enter the house; but it is nonsense: pure absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily settled, if it is,\u201d observed Duff.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is perfectly right,\u201d said Blathers, nodding in confirmation and idly handling the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall from the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly not,\u201d replied the doctor, casting an uneasy look at the two ladies. \u201cI know his entire history; but we may speak of that by and by. You would prefer first to see the spot where the thieves tried their hand, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d returned Mr. Blathers. \u201cWe had best inspect the premises first, and question the servants afterward. That is the regular course of business.\u201d\\n\\nLights were accordingly brought; and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and, in short, everyone else, entered the small room at the end of the passage and looked out through the window; then went round by the lawn and looked in through it; then had a candle passed out to examine the shutter; then a lantern to follow the footprints; and then a pitchfork to prod the bushes. When this had been done, amid the breathless attention of all present, they came indoors again; and Mr. Giles and Brittles were made to enact, in melodramatic fashion, their parts in the preceding night\u2019s events. They performed it some six times, contradicting one another in no more than one material point on the first occasion, and in no more than a dozen on the last. This result attained, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a lengthy consultation, beside which, in secrecy and gravity, a meeting of eminent physicians over the most difficult question in medicine would have been mere children\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced up and down the adjoining room in a state of great uneasiness; while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with anxious expressions.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after a great many very quick turns, \u201cI scarcely know what to do.\u201d\"}"
