          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"337d036c0d99aa5f6e3fab77\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, well, Mr. Bumble,\u201d he said at last, \u201cthere\u2019s no denying that, since the new feeding system was introduced, the coffins have become somewhat narrower and shallower than they used to be; but we must make some profit, Mr. Bumble. Properly seasoned timber is expensive, sir; and all the iron handles come by canal from Birmingham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, well,\u201d said Mr. Bumble, \u201cevery business has its disadvantages. A reasonable profit is, of course, permitted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course, of course,\u201d replied the undertaker; \u201cand if I don\u2019t make a profit on this particular item or that one, why, I recover it in the long run, you see\u2014he! he! he!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPrecisely,\u201d said Mr. Bumble.\\n\\n\u201cThough I must say,\u201d continued the undertaker, returning to the line of thought the beadle had interrupted, \u201cthough I must say, Mr. Bumble, that I have one very serious disadvantage to contend with: all the stout people die the soonest. Those who have been better off, and paid rates for many years, are the first to fail when they enter the house; and let me tell you, Mr. Bumble, that three or four inches beyond one\u2019s estimate makes a considerable dent in one\u2019s profits\u2014especially when one has a family to support, sir.\u201d\\n\\nAs Mr. Sowerberry said this with the proper indignation of a badly treated man, and as Mr. Bumble felt it seemed to cast a reflection on the parish\u2019s honour, the latter gentleman thought it wise to change the subject. Oliver Twist was foremost in his thoughts, and he made him the subject.\\n\\n\u201cBy the way,\u201d said Mr. Bumble, \u201cyou don\u2019t happen to know anyone who wants a boy, do you? A parish apprentice, who is currently a dead weight\u2014a millstone, one might say, around the parish neck? Generous terms, Mr. Sowerberry, generous terms?\u201d As Mr. Bumble spoke, he lifted his cane toward the notice above him and struck the words \u201cfive pounds\u201d three times; they were printed there in enormous Roman capitals.\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens!\u201d said the undertaker, taking Mr. Bumble by the gold-trimmed lapel of his official coat. \u201cThat is exactly what I wanted to speak to you about. You know\u2014dear me, what an elegant button that is, Mr. Bumble! I had never noticed it before.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I think it\u2019s rather handsome,\u201d said the beadle, looking proudly down at the large brass buttons decorating his coat. \u201cThe design is the same as the parish seal\u2014the Good Samaritan tending the sick and injured man. The board gave it to me on New Year\u2019s morning, Mr. Sowerberry. I remember putting it on for the first time when I attended the inquest on that ruined tradesman who died in a doorway at midnight.\u201d\"}"
