          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"97bb60c187f8b657fcf18662\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Suddenly Mr. Podgers let go of Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand and caught his left, bending so close to inspect it that the gold rims of his spectacles seemed almost to touch the palm. For a moment his face turned white with horror, but he quickly regained his composure and, looking up at Lady Windermere, said with a strained smile, \u2018It is the hand of a charming young man.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course it is!\u2019 replied Lady Windermere. \u2018But will he be a charming husband? That is what I want to know.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018All charming young men are,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u2018I don\u2019t think a husband ought to be too fascinating,\u2019 murmured Lady Jedburgh thoughtfully. \u2018It is so dangerous.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear child, they never are too fascinating,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere. \u2018But I want details. Details are the only things that interest me. What is going to happen to Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, within the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh yes, his honeymoon, of course!\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And lose a relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not his sister, I hope?\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh in a sorrowful voice.\\n\\n\u2018Certainly not his sister,\u2019 answered Mr. Podgers, waving his hand dismissively. \u2018Only a distant relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, I am terribly disappointed,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018I have absolutely nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. Nobody cares about distant relatives nowadays. They went out of fashion years ago. Still, I suppose she had better keep a black silk dress ready; it is always suitable for church, you know. And now let us go to supper. They are sure to have eaten everything, but perhaps we may find some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois used to make excellent soup, but he is so upset about politics at present that I am never quite sure of him. I do wish General Boulanger would keep quiet. Duchess, I am sure you are tired?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not at all, dear Gladys,\u2019 answered the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have enjoyed myself immensely, and the foot doctor\u2014I mean the palm reader\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where can my tortoiseshell fan be? Oh, thank you so much, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind, I\u2019m sure\u2019; and the good woman finally managed to get downstairs without dropping her scent bottle more than twice.\\n\\nAll this time Lord Arthur Savile had stood by the fireplace, still filled with dread and the sickening feeling that evil was approaching. He smiled sadly at his sister as she passed him on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, lovely in her pink brocade and pearls, and he barely heard Lady Windermere call for him to follow. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the thought that anything might come between them brought tears to his eyes.\"}"
