e conversation, as though she were a regular member of the household.\\n\\nWhen Carton came in, sat down, and asked, in very poor French, for a small glass of wine, Madame Defarge gave him a careless look, then a sharper one, then sharper still. She came over to him herself and asked what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated what he had already said.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d Madame Defarge asked, lifting her dark eyebrows with curiosity.\\n\\nAfter looking at her as though even one French word took time to form, he replied in his former heavy foreign accent.\"}"
