          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cb06aa0fe0385e04ca204eaa\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Tom managed to scratch up the cupboard with it, and was preparing to start on the bureau when he was called away to dress for Sunday school.\\n\\nMary gave him a tin basin of water and a piece of soap. He went outside the door and set the basin on a small bench; then he dipped the soap in the water and put it down, rolled up his sleeves, gently poured the water onto the ground, and went into the kitchen to rub his face industriously on the towel behind the door. But Mary took the towel away and said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, aren\u2019t you ashamed, Tom? You mustn\u2019t be so bad. Water won\u2019t hurt you.\u201d\\n\\nTom was somewhat unsettled. The basin was filled again, and this time he stood over it for a while, gathering courage; then he drew a deep breath and began. When he came into the kitchen shortly afterward, both eyes shut and his hands feeling for the towel, an honorable proof of soap suds and water dripped from his face. But when he emerged from the towel, he still was not satisfactory, for the clean area ended abruptly at his chin and jaws, like a mask; below and beyond that line lay a dark stretch of unwatered soil, running down his front and around the back of his neck. Mary took charge of him, and when she had finished, he was a man and a brother, with no distinction of color; his soaked hair was neatly brushed, its short curls arranged into a delicate, symmetrical effect. He secretly worked the curls flat, with effort and difficulty, plastering his hair close to his head, for he considered curls effeminate, and his own made his life bitter. Then Mary brought out a suit he had worn only on Sundays for two years\u2014simply called his \u201cother clothes\u201d\u2014which tells us the size of his wardrobe. After he dressed, the girl put him in order: she buttoned his tidy roundabout to his chin, folded his enormous shirt collar down over his shoulders, brushed him off, and set his speckled straw hat on his head. He looked greatly improved and uncomfortable. He was every bit as uncomfortable as he appeared, for there was a restriction in whole clothes and cleanliness that irritated him. He hoped Mary would forget his shoes, but that hope was ruined; as was customary, she thoroughly coated them with tallow and brought them out. He lost his temper and said he was always being forced to do everything he did not want to do.\"}"
