ondering why people liked her so much. The thought of Mr. Elton certainly cheered her; but after a while, her tender heart turned again toward the rejected Mr. Martin.\\n\\n\u201cNow he has received my letter,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI wonder what they are all doing\u2014whether his sisters know\u2014if he is unhappy, they will be unhappy too. I hope he will not take it so very much to heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet us think of our absent friends who may be more happily occupied,\u201d cried Emma. \u201cAt this very moment, perhaps, Mr. Elton is showing your picture to his mother and sisters, telling them how much more beautiful the original is, and, after they have asked five or six times, allowing them to hear your name\u2014your own dear name.\u201d\"}"
