          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d057993374800816b18cda2d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"For a moment I was too astonished to think clearly. I knew my own design differed greatly from this one in its details, though there was some general resemblance. Soon I took a candle, sat at the far end of the room, and examined the parchment more carefully. When I turned it over, I saw my own sketch on the other side, exactly as I had drawn it. At first I was simply amazed by the striking similarity of their outlines\u2014the strange coincidence that, without my knowing it, there had been a skull on the reverse of the parchment, directly beneath my drawing of the scarab\u00e6us, and that this skull resembled my sketch so closely, not only in shape but in size. The oddness of this coincidence completely stunned me for a while. Such coincidences often have that effect. The mind tries to find a connection, a chain of cause and effect, and when it cannot, it suffers a kind of temporary paralysis. But when I recovered from this shock, an idea slowly came to me that startled me far more than the coincidence itself. I began to remember clearly and firmly that there had been no drawing on the parchment when I made my sketch of the scarab\u00e6us. I became completely certain of it, because I remembered turning over first one side and then the other, looking for the cleanest place. If the skull had been there then, I could not possibly have missed it. This was truly a mystery I could not explain; yet even at that early moment, deep in the most hidden parts of my mind, there seemed to flicker a faint, glow-worm-like idea of the truth that last night\u2019s adventure proved so wonderfully. I rose at once, put the parchment safely away, and put off all further thought until I was alone.\\n\\n\u201cWhen you had left, and Jupiter was sound asleep, I began a more orderly investigation of the matter. First, I considered how the parchment had come into my hands. The place where we found the scarab\u00e6us was on the mainland coast, about a mile east of the island and only a short distance above the high-water mark. When I picked it up, it bit me sharply, making me drop it. Jupiter, with his usual caution, before taking hold of the insect, which had flown toward him, looked around for a leaf or something similar with which to grasp it.\"}"
