          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"57e6ab879111b4552c54afde\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When Mr. Hiram B. Otis, the American Minister, bought Canterville Chase, everyone told him he was doing a very foolish thing, because the house was certainly haunted. Lord Canterville himself, a man of the strictest honour, felt obliged to tell Mr. Otis about it when they began discussing the sale.\\n\\n\u2018We have not lived there ourselves,\u2019 said Lord Canterville, \u2018since my great-aunt, the Dowager Duchess of Bolton, was so frightened by two skeleton hands being laid on her shoulders while she was dressing for dinner that she suffered a fit and never truly recovered. I feel bound to tell you, Mr. Otis, that the ghost has been seen by several living members of my family, as well as by the parish rector, the Rev. Augustus Dampier, a Fellow of King\u2019s College, Cambridge. After the Duchess\u2019s unfortunate accident, none of our younger servants would remain with us, and Lady Canterville often slept very little at night because of the mysterious noises from the corridor and the library.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My Lord,\u2019 replied the Minister, \u2018I will take the furniture and the ghost at a fair price. I come from a modern country, where we have everything money can buy; and with all our lively young men taking over the Old World, carrying off your best actresses and opera singers, I reckon that if Europe had such a thing as a ghost, we would soon have one at home in a public museum or travelling about as a show.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am afraid the ghost does exist,\u2019 said Lord Canterville, smiling, \u2018though it may have refused the offers of your energetic showmen. It has been well known for three centuries\u2014since 1584, in fact\u2014and it always appears before the death of a member of our family.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, the family doctor does that too, Lord Canterville. But there is no such thing as a ghost, sir, and I suppose the laws of Nature are not going to be broken for the British aristocracy.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You are certainly very natural in America,\u2019 replied Lord Canterville, who did not quite understand Mr. Otis\u2019s last remark, \u2018and if you do not mind having a ghost in the house, that is all right. Only remember that I warned you.\u2019\\n\\nA few weeks later, the purchase was completed, and at the end of the season the Minister and his family went down to Canterville Chase. Mrs. Otis, who as Miss Lucretia R. Tappan of West 53rd Street had been a famous New York beauty, was now a very handsome middle-aged woman, with fine eyes and a superb profile.\"}"
