ame out at that time, and she loved him passionately. There is no doubt that she completely idolized him. He exploited her affection so methodically that he obtained large sums of money from her, and persuaded her to buy her brother\u2019s share in the brewery\u2014which his father had unwisely left him\u2014at an enormous price, claiming that, once he was her husband, he must own and manage the whole concern. Your guardian was not then among Miss Havisham\u2019s confidants, and she was too proud and too much in love to accept advice from anyone.\"}"
