ng about fifty gallons, along with one larger cask; six properly shaped tubes of tinned metal, three inches wide and ten feet long; a quantity of a certain metal, or semi-metal, which I will not name; and a dozen demijohns of a very common acid. The gas produced from these last materials has never, to my knowledge, been made by anyone but myself\u2014or at least never used for a similar purpose. I would readily reveal the secret, except that it properly belongs to a citizen of Nantz, France, who shared it with me only on certain conditions.\"}"
