gnized by both, and by Elizabeth more graciously than before. She spoke to him once, and glanced at him more than once. Elizabeth was, in truth, considering an important step. What followed made it clear. After spending a few minutes on the requisite civil nothings, she began to offer the invitation intended to include all that remained due to the Musgroves: \u201cTo-morrow evening, to meet a few friends; no formal party.\u201d She delivered it all with great grace, and the cards she had brought with her\u2014\u201cMiss Elliot at home\u201d\u2014were placed upon the table, accompanied by a polite, inclusive smile for all, and a smile and card more particularly directed to Captain Wentworth. The fact was that Elizabeth had been in Bath long enough to recognize the value of a man with such an air and appearance as his.\"}"
