          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4530263919f469a56e93db12\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Of course, he was very entertaining and all that, but I was terribly disappointed; and when I asked him about the coat of mail, he merely laughed and said it was much too cold to wear in England. Ah, here is Mr. Podgers! Now, Mr. Podgers, I want you to read the Duchess of Paisley\u2019s hand. Duchess, you must take off your glove. No, not the left hand\u2014the other one.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Gladys, I really do not think it is quite proper,\u2019 said the Duchess, weakly unfastening a rather dirty kid glove.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing interesting ever is,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018_On a fait le monde ainsi_. But I must introduce you. Duchess, this is Mr. Podgers, my favourite palm-reader. Mr. Podgers, this is the Duchess of Paisley, and if you say she has a larger mount of the moon than I do, I shall never believe in you again.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am sure, Gladys, there is nothing of that sort in my hand,\u2019 said the Duchess solemnly.\\n\\n\u2018Your Grace is quite right,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, looking at the small fat hand with its short, square fingers. \u2018The mount of the moon is undeveloped. The life line, however, is excellent. Kindly bend your wrist. Thank you. Three distinct lines on the _rascette_! You will live to a great age, Duchess, and be extremely happy. Ambition\u2014very moderate; intellect line not excessive; heart line\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Now do be indiscreet, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing would please me more,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, bowing, \u2018if the Duchess had ever been so; but I regret to say that I see great constancy of affection, joined to a strong sense of duty.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Please continue, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 said the Duchess, looking quite pleased.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is not the least of Your Grace\u2019s virtues,\u2019 Mr. Podgers continued, and Lady Windermere burst into laughter.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is an