{"request_id":"8708326f8c004fcfebf237fd","rewritten_text":"As I passed my hand through the valve, carrying a cup of water for the old cat, my shirt sleeves caught in the loop supporting the basket and, in an instant, loosened it from the bottom. If the whole thing had vanished into thin air, it could not have disappeared from my sight more suddenly. Truly, not a tenth of a second could have passed between the basket’s release and its complete disappearance, with everything in it. My good wishes followed it down to earth, but naturally I had no hope that either the cat or her kittens would survive to tell of their misfortune.

“At six o’clock, I saw a large part of the earth’s visible surface to the east covered in deep shadow, which advanced with great speed until, at five minutes before seven, the entire landscape in view was wrapped in the darkness of night. Yet it was long after this before the setting sun’s rays stopped illuminating the balloon; and this, though I had fully expected it, gave me immense pleasure. It was clear that in the morning I would see the rising sun at least several hours before the citizens of Rotterdam, despite their being so much farther east; and so, day after day, as I rose higher, I would enjoy sunlight for longer and longer periods. I then decided to keep a journal of my journey, counting each day as a continuous twenty-four hours, without regard to the intervals of darkness.

“At ten o’clock, feeling drowsy, I decided to lie down for the rest of the night; but then a difficulty arose which, obvious as it may seem, had escaped me until that very moment. If I slept as I intended, how could the air in the chamber be renewed in the meantime? Breathing it for more than an hour at most would be impossible; or, even if that time could be stretched to an hour and a quarter, the most disastrous consequences might follow. This dilemma caused me considerable anxiety; and it will scarcely be believed that, after the dangers I had already faced, I regarded the matter so seriously that I abandoned all hope of achieving my final purpose and resolved that I must descend. But this hesitation lasted only a moment."}

