egret. \u201cNot one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what are you talking about?\u201d Fagin answered angrily. \u201cWhat are you crying for?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBecause it won\u2019t be on the rec-ord, will it?\u201d said Charley, driven into open defiance of his old friend by the force of his sorrow. \u201cBecause it can\u2019t come out in the in-dictment; because nobody will ever know half of what he was. How will he appear in the Newgate Calendar? Perhaps he won\u2019t be there at all. Oh, my eye, my eye, what a blow it is!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d cried Fagin, holding out his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter in a fit of laughter that shook him as if he had palsy. \u201cSee what pride they take in their profession, my dear.\u201d\"}"
