elf-important pretence of astonishment, that she could not help responding sharply,\\n\\n\u201cMr. Elton, this is the most extraordinary behaviour! I can explain it in only one way: you are not yourself, or you could not speak to me, or of Harriet, in such a manner. Control yourself enough to say no more, and I will try to forget it.\u201d\\n\\nBut Mr. Elton had drunk only enough wine to raise his spirits, not enough to cloud his mind. He knew perfectly well what he meant; and after strongly protesting that her suspicion was deeply unfair, and briefly referring to his regard for Miss Smith as her friend\u2014while admitting his astonishment that Miss Smith should be mentioned at all\u2014he returned to the subject of his own passion and pressed urgently for a favourable answer.\"}"
