cked fast, with the key cast away.\\n\\nA figure now slipped stealthily through an opening at the far end of the ruined building, but they failed to see it.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d Huckleberry whispered, \u201cdoes this stop us from _ever_ telling\u2014_always_?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course it does. It don\u2019t matter _what_ happens, we have to keep quiet. We\u2019d drop down dead\u2014don\u2019t _you_ know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I suppose that\u2019s right.\u201d\\n\\nThey went on whispering for a while. Soon a dog began a long, mournful howl just outside\u2014no more than ten feet from them. The boys suddenly clutched one another in a panic of terror.\\n\\n\u201cWhich one of us does he mean?\u201d Huckleberry gasped.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014look through the crack. Quick!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, _you_, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t _do_ it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
