r would keep quiet. Duchess, I am sure you must be tired?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not at all, dear Gladys,\u2019 replied the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have enjoyed myself immensely, and the cheiropodist\u2014I mean the cheiromantist\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where can my tortoiseshell fan be? Oh, thank you so much, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind, I\u2019m sure\u2019; and the worthy woman finally managed to get downstairs without dropping her scent bottle more than twice.\\n\\nAll this time Lord Arthur Savile had remained by the fireplace, gripped by the same dread, the same sickening sense of approaching evil. He smiled sadly at his sister as she swept past him on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, lovely in her pink brocade and pearls, and he scarcely heard Lady Windermere call for him to follow. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the thought that anything might come between them brought tears to his eyes.\"}"
