          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ec5079e9006617beb5c93689\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She was right concerning the rats. Every now and then you could see one poke his nose from a hole in the corner. She said she needed to keep things close by to fling at them when she was alone, else they wouldn\u2019t leave her any peace. She showed me a bar of lead bent into a knot, and said she was generally a good hand with it, but she\u2019d strained her arm a day or two before, and couldn\u2019t tell whether she could throw straight now. Still, she waited for an opening, and presently let fly at a rat; but she missed him by a good ways, and cried, \u201cOuch!\u201d because her arm hurt so. Then she told me to take the next one. I wanted to be gone before the old man came back, but naturally I didn\u2019t show it. I took the thing, and when the first rat put out his nose I sent it after him, and if he\u2019d stayed put he\u2019d have been a pretty sick rat. She said that was splendid, and reckoned I\u2019d get the next one. She went off and picked up the lead, brought it back, and fetched a hank of yarn besides, which she wanted my help with. I held up both hands, and she slipped the hank over them, talking all the while about her own and her husband\u2019s affairs. But she stopped short to say:\\n\\n\u201cWatch the rats. You\u2019d better keep the lead in your lap, where it\u2019s handy.\u201d\\n\\nSo she dropped the lump into my lap that very instant, and I squeezed my knees together over it while she kept talking. But not for more than a minute. Then she took the hank away, looked me square in the face, pleasant as could be, and said:\\n\\n\u201cNow then, what\u2019s your true name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWh\u2014what, mum?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat is your true name? Is it Bill, or Tom, or Bob\u2014or what?\u201d\\n\\nI reckon I trembled like a leaf, and scarcely knew what to do. But I said:\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t make sport of a poor girl like me, mum. If I\u2019m in your way, I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you won\u2019t. Sit down and remain where you are. I\u2019m not going to harm you, and I\u2019m not going to give you away, neither. Just tell me your secret and trust me. I\u2019ll keep it; and more than that, I\u2019ll help you. My old man will too, if you need him. You\u2019re a runaway \u2019prentice, that\u2019s all. It ain\u2019t much. There\u2019s no harm in it. You\u2019ve been badly used, and made up your mind to run. Bless you, child, I wouldn\u2019t tell on you.\"}"
