h I appeal to an angelic judge. I cannot leave without your forgiveness, and I must try to win it, or else despair. I beg you, therefore, to listen to my words; and if guilt may in any degree be softened by severe agony and remorse that tears the mind like madness, perhaps you may think\u2014though I dare not\u2014that I have some claim upon your compassion.\\n\\n\u201cI beg you to remember our first happy life on the shores of Loch Lomond. I had returned from sixteen years of weary wandering, during which, though I had endured many dangers and misfortunes, my affections had remained entirely blank.\"}"
