st ended, there came a knock at the door. Huck sprang toward a hiding-place, for he had no wish to be connected, even distantly, with the recent affair. The Welshman let in several ladies and gentlemen, including the Widow Douglas, and observed groups of townspeople climbing the hill\u2014to look at the stile. The news had spread, then. The Welshman had to relate the night\u2019s story to the visitors. The widow spoke openly of her gratitude for being saved.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t mention it, madam. There\u2019s another you may be more indebted to than to me and my boys, perhaps, but he won\u2019t let me tell his name. We wouldn\u2019t have been there without him.\u201d\"}"
