          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2c08016c5ce383f14a63e0f2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Dearest Rose, just one more!\u201d cried Harry, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world would call it\u2014if I had been destined for some quiet, obscure life\u2014if I had been poor, ill, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or has the prospect of my rising to wealth and honour created this hesitation?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe question does not apply, and never will. It is unfair, almost cruel, to press it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I scarcely dare hope it is,\u201d Harry returned, \u201cit will cast a ray of happiness over my lonely path and light the road ahead. It is no small thing to give so much, with only a few brief words, to someone who loves you above everything else. Oh, Rose, in the name of my passionate and lasting devotion; in the name of all I have suffered for you, and all you condemn me to suffer; answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your circumstances had been different,\u201d Rose answered, \u201cif you had been only a little, but not so greatly, above me; if I could have been a help and comfort to you in some humble life of peace and seclusion, rather than a stain and burden among ambitious and distinguished people; I would have been spared this ordeal. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now; but then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs Rose made this confession, memories of old hopes she had cherished as a girl long ago crowded into her mind. But they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return withered; and the tears relieved her.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot help this weakness, and it only strengthens my resolve,\u201d said Rose, holding out her hand. \u201cI truly must leave you now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask one promise,\u201d Harry said. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014within a year, though it may be much sooner\u2014I may speak to you again on this subject, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to urge me to change my proper decision,\u201d Rose replied with a sorrowful smile. \u201cThat would be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnly to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it finally. I will place at your feet whatever rank or fortune I may have; and if you still hold to your present decision, I will not try, by word or deed, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cIt is only one more pain, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand again.\"}"
