          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"864c34193a356a9011c2a4c9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He bowed, then took his leave. At that moment he saw no one in the street. It is a side street\u2014exceedingly solitary.\\n\\n\u201c_William Bird_, tailor, deposes that he was among the party which entered the house. Is an Englishman. Has resided in Paris for two years. Was one of the earliest to go up the stairs. Heard the voices in dispute. The rough voice was French. Could distinguish several words, though cannot now recall them all. Heard plainly \u2018_sacr\u00e9_\u2019 and \u2018_mon Dieu._\u2019 At the same instant there was a noise as of several persons in a struggle\u2014a sound of scraping and scuffling. The shrill voice was very loud\u2014louder than the rough one. Is certain it was not an Englishman\u2019s voice. Seemed to be that of a German. It might have been a woman\u2019s voice. Does not understand German.\\n\\n\u201cFour of the witnesses above mentioned, being recalled, deposed that the chamber door in which Mademoiselle L.\u2019s body was discovered was locked from within when the party arrived. All was entirely silent\u2014there were no groans nor sounds of any description. When the door was forced, no person was visible. The windows of both the rear and front rooms were lowered and securely fastened on the inside. A door connecting the two rooms was shut, though not locked. The door from the front room into the passage was locked, the key being inside. A small room at the front of the house, on the fourth floor and at the passage head, stood open, its door partly ajar. This room was filled with old bedsteads, boxes, and the like. These were removed and examined with care. Not a single inch of any part of the house escaped careful search. Sweeps were sent up and down the chimneys. The house had four stories, with garrets (_mansardes._) A trap-door in the roof was very firmly nailed down\u2014apparently unopened for years. The interval between the voices being heard in contention and the forcing of the chamber door was differently estimated by the witnesses. Some placed it at as little as three minutes\u2014others at as much as five. The door was opened only with difficulty.\\n\\n\u201c_Alfonzo Garcio_, undertaker, deposes that he lives in the Rue Morgue. Is a Spaniard by birth. Was one of the party entering the house. Did not go upstairs. Is of a nervous disposition, and feared the effects of agitation. Heard the voices in dispute. The rough voice was French. Could not make out the words spoken. The shrill voice was that of an Englishman\u2014is positive of it.\"}"
