{"request_id":"f613ca45ea372b00f542021a","rewritten_text":"As I passed my hand through the valve, carrying a cup of water for the old cat, my shirt sleeves caught in the loop that held up the basket and, in an instant, pulled it loose from the bottom. If it had vanished into thin air, it could not have disappeared from my sight more suddenly. Truly, not even a tenth of a second passed between the basket’s release and its complete disappearance, along with everything in it. My good wishes followed it down to earth, but naturally I had no hope that either the cat or her kittens would survive to tell of their misfortune.

“At six o’clock, I saw a large part of the visible earth to the east covered in deep shadow. The shadow moved forward very quickly, until, at five minutes before seven, the entire surface I could see was wrapped in the darkness of night. Yet the setting sun continued to shine on the balloon for a long time afterward. Though I had expected this, it gave me great pleasure. It was clear that in the morning I would see the sun rise many hours before the people of Rotterdam, despite their being so much farther east. Thus, day after day, as I rose higher, I would enjoy sunlight for longer and longer periods. I then decided to keep a journal of my journey, counting each day as a continuous twenty-four hours, without regard to the periods of darkness.

“At ten o’clock, feeling sleepy, I decided to lie down for the rest of the night. But then a problem arose, obvious though it was, that had escaped my notice until that very moment. If I slept as I intended, how could the air in the chamber be renewed while I slept? Breathing it for more than an hour at most would be impossible; and even if that time could be stretched to an hour and a quarter, the consequences might be disastrous. This difficulty troubled me greatly. It will scarcely be believed that, after all the dangers I had faced, I took this matter so seriously that I gave up hope of achieving my final purpose and decided I would have to descend. But this hesitation lasted only a moment."}

