y arisen only from playfulness or whim, but it now took on a harsh and earnest character. When Jupiter again tried to muzzle him, he resisted furiously and, springing into the pit, clawed up the earth in a frenzy. Within seconds he had laid bare a heap of human bones: two entire skeletons, mingled with several metal buttons and what seemed the dust of rotten woollen cloth. A stroke or two of a spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife; and, as we dug deeper, three or four scattered pieces of gold and silver coin appeared.\"}"
