          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6ba87b01044da8538cef48d2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOh, I misunderstood you. I thought you said \u2018anybody,\u2019 and so I supposed \u2018anybody\u2019 meant\u2014well, anybody; that is, everybody.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does\u2014anybody of high birth; and all the better if he be royal.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat seems reasonable,\u201d said the abbot, seeing his chance to calm things and prevent disaster, \u201cfor it is not likely that such a marvelous gift would be granted to reveal the affairs of lesser people rather than those born near the heights of greatness. Our King Arthur\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWould you know of him?\u201d the enchanter interrupted.\\n\\n\u201cMost gladly, yes, and gratefully.\u201d\\n\\nAt once everybody was full of awe and interest again, the hopeless idiots. They watched the spells with deep attention, and when the announcement came, they looked at me as if to say, \u201cThere, now, what can you say to that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe king is tired from the hunt, and has lain in his palace these two hours, sleeping without dreams.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod\u2019s blessing upon him!\u201d said the abbot, crossing himself. \u201cMay that sleep refresh both his body and his soul.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd it might, if he were asleep,\u201d I said, \u201cbut the king is not sleeping. The king is riding.\u201d\\n\\nThere was trouble again\u2014a clash of authority. No one knew which of us to believe; I still had some reputation left. The magician was stirred to scorn, and said:\\n\\n\u201cLook, I have seen many wonderful seers, prophets, and magicians in my lifetime, but never one before who could sit idle and see into the heart of things without a single spell to help him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have lived in the woods, and lost much by it. I use spells myself, as this good brotherhood knows\u2014but only on important occasions.\u201d\\n\\nWhen it comes to sarcasm, I reckon I can hold my own. That thrust made the fellow squirm. The abbot asked about the queen and the court, and received this answer:\\n\\n\u201cThey are all asleep, overcome by weariness, just as the king is.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cThat is simply another lie. Half of them are enjoying themselves; the queen and the other half are not asleep, they are riding. Now perhaps you can show us what you can do, and tell us where the king and queen, and all those riding with them at this moment, are going?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey sleep now, as I said; but tomorrow they will ride, for they are taking a journey toward the sea.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd where will they be the day after tomorrow at vespers?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFar north of Camelot, with half their journey completed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is another lie, by a hundred and fifty miles.\u201d\"}"
