          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"71cc2c63e1665f95148d67ea\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhy, you surely don\u2019t mean\u2014\u201d my sister began.\\n\\n\u201cYes, I do, Mum,\u201d said Pumblechook; \u201cbut hold a moment. Go on, Joseph. That\u2019s right! Go on!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would present company say,\u201d Joe continued, \u201cto twenty pound?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHandsome is the word,\u201d my sister replied.\\n\\n\u201cWell then,\u201d said Joe, \u201cit\u2019s above twenty pound.\u201d\\n\\nThat low hypocrite Pumblechook nodded once more, saying with a condescending laugh, \u201cMore than that, Mum. Right again! Press her, Joseph!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, to have done with it,\u201d said Joe, joyfully putting the bag into my sister\u2019s hand, \u201cit\u2019s five-and-twenty pound.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is five-and-twenty pound, Mum,\u201d repeated that most infamous swindler, Pumblechook, getting up to shake hands with her; \u201cand it is only what your merits deserve (as I said when I was consulted), and I wish you joy of the money!\u201d\\n\\nHad the rascal stopped there, his conduct would have been bad enough; but he deepened his offence by taking me into custody, with a patronizing authority that made all his earlier villainy seem slight.\\n\\n\u201cNow, you see, Joseph and wife,\u201d said Pumblechook, taking hold of my arm above the elbow, \u201cI\u2019m one of those who always carry through whatever they begin. This boy must be bound, straight away. That is _my_ method. Bound straight away.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGoodness knows, Uncle Pumblechook,\u201d said my sister, clutching the money, \u201cwe are greatly obliged to you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever trouble about me, Mum,\u201d answered that devilish cornchandler. \u201cA pleasure is a pleasure everywhere. But the boy, you understand; he must be bound. I said I would attend to it\u2014to speak plainly.\u201d\\n\\nThe Justices were sitting at the Town Hall close by, and we immediately crossed over to have me bound apprentice to Joe in the Magistrates\u2019 presence. I say we crossed over, though Pumblechook pushed me across, precisely as if I had just picked a pocket or set fire to a rick; indeed, the general belief in Court was that I had been caught in the act. As Pumblechook thrust me ahead of him through the crowd, I heard some say, \u201cWhat has he done?\u201d and others, \u201cHe\u2019s only a young \u2019un, but he looks a bad one, don\u2019t he?\u201d One mild-looking, benevolent person even handed me a tract, decorated with a woodcut of a wicked young man equipped with a complete sausage-shop of fetters, and called TO BE READ IN MY CELL.\\n\\nThe Hall seemed a strange place to me, with loftier pews than a church had,\u2014people leaning over them to watch,\u2014and imposing Justices (one with a powdered head) reclining in chairs with folded arms, taking snuff, falling asleep, writing, or reading newspapers,\u2014and glossy black portraits upon the walls, which my untrained eye took for a mixture of hardbake and sticking-plaster.\"}"
