          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f1a339272ea04b567f3308a6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJoseph!! Joseph!!!\u201d At that, he shook his head and tapped it, to show what he thought Joseph lacked.\\n\\n\u201cBut, my dear young friend,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, \u201cyou must be hungry, you must be worn out. Sit down. Here is a chicken sent round from the Boar, here is a tongue sent round from the Boar, here are one or two small matters sent round from the Boar, which I trust you will not scorn. But do I,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again almost as soon as he had seated himself, \u201cbehold afore me, him as I used to sport with in the days of his happy infancy? And may I\u2014_may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nThis May I meant, might he shake hands? I gave permission, and he was ardent, after which he sat down once more.\\n\\n\u201cHere is wine,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook. \u201cLet us drink, Thanks to Fortune, and may she always choose her favourites with as much judgment! Yet I cannot,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, getting up again, \u201cbehold afore me One\u2014and drink likewise to One\u2014without once more expressing\u2014May I\u2014_may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nI told him he might, and he shook hands with me again, drained his glass, and set it upside down. I did likewise; and had I been turned upside down before I drank, the wine could scarcely have gone more straight to my head.\\n\\nMr. Pumblechook served me the liver wing and the choicest slice of tongue (none of those remote No Thoroughfares of Pork now), while, comparatively, taking no thought for himself. \u201cAh! poultry, poultry! You never imagined,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, addressing the fowl upon the dish, \u201cwhen you was a young fledgling, what fate awaited you. You never imagined you was to be refreshment beneath this humble roof for one as\u2014Call it weakness, if you please,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again, \u201cbut may I? _may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nIt was becoming needless to repeat the ceremony of saying he might, so he did it immediately. How he managed it so often without cutting himself on my knife, I cannot tell.\\n\\n\u201cAnd your sister,\u201d he went on, after a little uninterrupted eating, \u201cwhich had the honour of bringing you up by hand! It\u2019s a melancholy picter, to consider that she is no longer able fully to comprehend the honour. May\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI perceived that he was preparing to come at me again, and stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll drink her health,\u201d said I.\\n\\n\u201cAh!\u201d cried Mr. Pumblechook, reclining in his chair, quite limp with admiration, \u201cthat\u2019s how you know \u2019em, sir!\u201d (I don\u2019t know who Sir was, but it certainly was not I, and no third person was there); \u201cthat\u2019s how you know the noble-minded, sir!\u201d\"}"
