          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"53bf20bb2bc7ee183842db71\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you play?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think, sir,\u201d said the spy, in the most abject tone, turning to Mr. Lorry, \u201cI may appeal to a gentleman of your age and kindness, and ask you to put it to this other gentleman, so much younger than yourself, whether he can, under any circumstances, reconcile it with his position to play the Ace he has mentioned. I admit that I am a spy, and that it is considered a disreputable occupation\u2014though someone must do it; but this gentleman is no spy, so why should he lower himself by becoming one?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI play my Ace, Mr. Barsad,\u201d said Carton, answering for himself and looking at his watch, \u201cwithout the slightest hesitation, in a very few minutes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI would have hoped, gentlemen,\u201d said the spy, still trying to draw Mr. Lorry into the matter, \u201cthat your respect for my sister\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI could show no greater respect for your sister than by finally freeing her from her brother,\u201d said Sydney Carton.\\n\\n\u201cYou do not think so, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have completely made up my mind.\u201d\\n\\nThe spy\u2019s polished manner, strangely at odds with his deliberately rough clothing, and probably with his usual behavior, was checked and defeated by Carton\u2019s unreadable nature\u2014he was a mystery to men wiser and more honest than the spy. While Barsad was at a loss, Carton, returning to his earlier air of studying cards, said:\\n\\n\u201cAnd now that I think of it, I have a strong feeling that I hold another good card here, one not yet counted. That friend and fellow Sheep, who said he had been tending his flock in the country prisons\u2014who was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFrench. You do not know him,\u201d said the spy quickly.\\n\\n\u201cFrench, eh?\u201d Carton repeated thoughtfully, seeming not to notice him at all, though he echoed the word. \u201cWell, perhaps he was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe is, I assure you,\u201d said the spy. \u201cThough it is unimportant.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThough it is unimportant,\u201d Carton repeated in the same automatic manner. \u201cThough it is unimportant\u2014no, it is not important. No. Still, I know that face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI do not think so. I am certain not. It cannot be,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cIt-can\u2019t-be,\u201d Sydney Carton muttered, looking back in his mind and idly emptying his glass again\u2014fortunately, it was a small one. \u201cCan\u2019t-be. He spoke good French. Yet he seemed like a foreigner, I thought?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProvincial,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo. Foreign!\u201d Carton cried, striking the table with his open hand as understanding suddenly came to him. \u201cCly! In disguise, but the same man. We had that man before us at the Old Bailey.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow you are being hasty, sir,\u201d said Barsad, with a smile that made his aquiline nose tilt even farther to one side. \u201cThere, you truly give me an advantage over you.\u201d\"}"
        }
