per to join in the evening\u2019s amusement. She was rather surprised to find that he had no doubts at all on the subject and was far from fearing a rebuke from either the Archbishop or Lady Catherine de Bourgh for daring to dance.\\n\\n\u201cI am certainly not of the opinion,\u201d he said, \u201cthat a ball of this sort, given by a young man of good character to respectable people, can have any harmful effect. So far from objecting to dancing myself, I hope to be honoured by the hands of all my fair cousins during the evening. And I take this opportunity to ask for yours, Miss Elizabeth, for the first two dances in particular\u2014a preference which I trust my cousin Jane will understand correctly, and not take as any disrespect to her.\u201d\"}"
