          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"25a385408064714efde68212\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The elegant gentlemen of the highest birth wore small hanging ornaments that tinkled as they moved lazily; these golden chains rang like tiny precious bells. Between that ringing and the rustling of silk, brocade, and fine linen, there was a flutter in the air that seemed to blow Saint Antoine and its starving hunger far away.\\n\\nDress was the one certain charm for keeping everything in its proper place. Everyone was dressed for a Fancy Ball that was never meant to end. From the Palace of the Tuileries, through Monseigneur and the whole Court, through the Chambers, the Courts of Justice, and all society except the scarecrows, the Fancy Ball reached down even to the Common Executioner. To preserve the charm, he was required to perform his duties \u201cfrizzled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014the axe was seldom used\u2014Monsieur Paris, as his fellow professionals in the provinces called him, along with Monsieur Orleans and the rest, presided in this delicate costume. And who at Monseigneur\u2019s reception in that year of our Lord seventeen hundred and eighty could possibly doubt that a system founded on a frizzled, powdered hangman in gold lace, pumps, and white silk stockings would last until the stars themselves went out?\\n\\nAfter Monseigneur had relieved his four men of their loads and drunk his chocolate, he ordered the doors of the Holiest of Holies thrown open and came out. Then what obedience, what bowing and scraping, what flattery, what servility, what low humiliation! Nothing was left for Heaven in the way of bowing body and soul\u2014which may have been one reason why Monseigneur\u2019s worshippers never troubled Heaven.\\n\\nGiving a promising word here and a smile there, whispering to one fortunate slave and waving a hand to another, Monseigneur graciously passed through his rooms to the distant region called the Circumference of Truth. There he turned and came back, and in time had himself shut inside his sanctuary by the chocolate sprites, and was seen no more.\\n\\nThe display ended, the flutter in the air became a small storm, and the precious little bells rang down the stairs. Soon only one person remained from the whole crowd. With his hat beneath his arm and his snuff-box in his hand, he slowly walked among the mirrors toward the exit.\\n\\n\u201cI devote you,\u201d said this person, pausing at the last door and turning toward the sanctuary, \u201cto the Devil!\u201d\\n\\nThen he shook the snuff from his fingers as though shaking dust from his feet, and quietly went downstairs.\"}"
