 great drops of perspiration sprang out upon his yellow forehead like a poisonous dew, and his plump fingers became cold and moist.\\n\\nLord Arthur was quick to observe these unusual marks of disturbance, and for the first time in his life he felt afraid himself. His first impulse was to flee the room, but he checked it. Better to learn the worst, whatever it might be, than remain in this dreadful uncertainty.\\n\\n\u2018I am waiting, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 he said.\\n\\n\u2018We are all waiting,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere in her brisk, impatient way; but the cheiromantist gave no answer.\\n\\n\u2018I believe Arthur is going on the stage,\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh, \u2018and that, after your rebuke, Mr. Podgers is frightened to tell him so.\u2019\"}"
