          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ccd7cc2577c365b48b925056\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Biddy wept; the gathering dusk in the garden, the lane, and the stars beginning to appear, were dimmed to my own eyes.\\n\\n\u201cNothing was ever found out, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you know what has become of Orlick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI should suppose, from the colour of his clothes, that he works in the quarries.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen you have seen him, of course?\u2014Why are you looking at that dark tree in the lane?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI saw him there on the night she died.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd that was not the last time, either, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo; I have seen him there since we have been walking here.\u2014It is useless,\u201d said Biddy, putting her hand on my arm as I was about to run out, \u201cyou know I would not mislead you; he was not there for a minute, and he has gone.\u201d\\n\\nIt renewed my deepest indignation to learn that she was still haunted by this fellow, and I felt bitterly hostile towards him. I said so, and declared that I would spend whatever money or effort was needed to drive him from that part of the country. Gradually she brought me to calmer conversation, and told me how Joe loved me, and how Joe never complained of anything,\u2014she did not say, of me; she need not have done so; I understood her meaning,\u2014but always performed his duty in his station of life, with a strong hand, a quiet tongue, and a tender heart.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, it would be difficult to praise him too highly,\u201d said I; \u201cand Biddy, we must speak of these matters often, for naturally I shall be down here frequently now. I am not going to leave poor Joe by himself.\u201d\\n\\nBiddy did not say one word.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy, do you not hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Mr. Pip.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLeaving aside your calling me Mr. Pip,\u2014which seems to me in poor taste, Biddy,\u2014what do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do I mean?\u201d Biddy asked, timidly.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d said I, with virtuous self-assertion, \u201cI must ask you to tell me what you mean by this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d said Biddy.\\n\\n\u201cNow, do not echo,\u201d I replied. \u201cYou did not use to echo, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid not use!\u201d said Biddy. \u201cO Mr. Pip! Did not use!\u201d\\n\\nWell! I thought I had better abandon that point too. After another quiet turn about the garden, I returned to the principal matter.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d said I, \u201cI remarked that I should come down here often, to see Joe, and you received it with marked silence. Be good enough, Biddy, to tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite certain, then, that you WILL come to see him often?\u201d asked Biddy, pausing in the narrow garden path and looking at me beneath the stars with clear, honest eyes.\"}"
