          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"109e53527c24bdf4ee00397b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I then went from shop to shop, buying whatever was needed to alter his appearance. When that business was done, I made my own way to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but when he saw me come in, he rose at once and stood before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. For as I had walked along, I had given careful thought to what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t commit yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t commit anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Tell me nothing: I want to know nothing; I am not curious.\u201d\\n\\nNaturally, I saw that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only wish, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make certain that what I have been informed is true. I have no hope that it is untrue, but I may at least confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head and looking not at me, but at the floor as though listening to it. \u201cTold would seem to suggest spoken communication. You cannot have spoken communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who was so long unknown to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd he alone?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd he alone,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you in any way responsible for my errors and mistaken conclusions; but I had always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d Mr. Jaggers replied, fixing his cool eyes on me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible for that at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it seemed so much like it, sir,\u201d I pleaded, my heart sinking.\\n\\n\u201cNot the smallest bit of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his coat-tails. \u201cJudge nothing by appearances; judge everything by evidence. There is no better rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I said with a sigh, after standing silent for a while. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, throughout all my dealings with you, I have kept to the exact line of fact. There has never been the slightest departure from that exact line of fact. You understand that fully?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFully, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI told Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must not expect me ever to depart from the exact line of fact.\u201d\"}"
