efore their complete union. Woodville continued to rise in fame, and Elinor grew lovelier and wiser under the guidance of her accomplished lover.\\n\\nIn two months Elinor would be twenty-one, and everything was ready for their marriage. How can I tell of disaster after so much joy? Yet the earth would not be the earth it is, covered with suffering and sorrow, if such a pair of angelic beings had been allowed to live for one another. Search the world, and you will not find the perfect happiness their marriage would have given them. The order of things among us miserable people of earth would have needed to be changed to allow such complete joy.\"}"
