her things needed for his terrible task. He began to wonder whether he and Basil Hallward had ever encountered one another and, if they had, what each had thought of the other.\\n\\n\u201cGo away now,\u201d said a harsh voice behind him.\\n\\nHe turned and rushed out, dimly aware that the dead man had been pushed back into the chair and that Campbell was staring at a shining yellow face. As he descended the stairs, he heard the key turn in the lock.\\n\\nIt was well past seven when Campbell returned to the library. He was pale, yet perfectly composed. \u201cI have done what you required of me,\u201d he muttered.\"}"
