          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"34ae102495ca6d3b21844fe4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"For a while I was too astonished to reason clearly. I knew my design differed greatly from this in its particulars\u2014though in its broad form there was some resemblance. At length I took a candle and, sitting at the farther end of the room, began to examine the parchment more minutely. Turning it over, I found my own sketch on the reverse, precisely as I had drawn it. My first thought was simply wonder at the extraordinary likeness of the outlines\u2014at the strange coincidence that, without my knowledge, a skull had existed on the other side of the parchment, directly beneath my drawing of the _scarab\u00e6us_, and that this skull should resemble my sketch so nearly, not merely in shape but in dimensions. The oddity of this coincidence, I repeat, completely bewildered me for a time. Such is the common effect of coincidences. The mind strives to discover a connexion\u2014a chain of cause and consequence\u2014and, failing in the effort, endures a kind of momentary paralysis. Yet, as I emerged from this stupor, a conviction slowly came upon me that alarmed me far more than the coincidence itself. I began clearly and firmly to recall that no drawing had been on the parchment when I made my sketch of the _scarab\u00e6us_. Of this I became wholly certain; for I remembered examining first one side, then the other, to find the cleanest place. Had the skull been there at that time, I could surely not have overlooked it. Here, indeed, was a mystery I felt unable to account for; but even in that first instant there appeared to flicker, faintly, in the deepest and most hidden recesses of my mind, a glow-worm-like notion of that truth which the adventure of last night afterward established so splendidly. I rose immediately and, having put the parchment safely away, put aside all further thought until I could be alone.\\n\\n\u201cWhen you had departed, and Jupiter was sound asleep, I set myself to a more systematic inquiry into the matter. First, I considered how the parchment had come into my hands. The place where we found the _scarab\u00e6us_ lay upon the mainland coast, roughly a mile east of the island, and only a little above the high-water mark. When I seized it, it bit me sharply, making me drop it. Jupiter, with his usual prudence, before taking hold of the insect, which had flown in his direction, searched about for a leaf, or something similar, with which to grasp it.\"}"
