y instantly ran, climbed the tall board fence, and vanished over it.\\n\\nAunt Polly stood astonished for a moment, then gave a soft laugh.\\n\\n\u201cConfound that boy, will I never learn? Hasn\u2019t he played enough tricks on me that I ought to be watching for them by now? But old fools are the greatest fools there are. You can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as they say. But goodness, he never plays the same trick two days running, and how is anyone supposed to know what\u2019s coming? He seems to know exactly how long he can torment me before I lose my temper, and he knows that if he can distract me for a minute or make me laugh, it all settles down again and I can\u2019t lay a hand on him.\u201d\"}"
