hether he would consider it proper to join in the evening\u2019s entertainment. She was rather surprised to discover that he had no scruples at all on the subject and was far from fearing a rebuke from either the Archbishop or Lady Catherine de Bourgh for daring to dance.\\n\\n\u201cI am certainly not of the opinion,\u201d he said, \u201cthat a ball of this sort, given by a young man of character to respectable people, can have any harmful effect; and so far am I from objecting to dancing myself that I hope to be honoured with the hands of all my lovely cousins during the evening. I take this opportunity, Miss Elizabeth, to request yours for the first two dances in particular\u2014a preference which I trust my cousin Jane will ascribe to its proper cause, and not to any disrespect toward her.\u201d\"}"
