and stood watching from a neighbouring portico.\\n\\n\u201cWhose house is that, Constable?\u201d asked the older of the two gentlemen.\\n\\n\u201cMr. Dorian Gray\u2019s, sir,\u201d replied the policeman.\\n\\nAs they walked away, they exchanged looks and sneered. One was Sir Henry Ashton\u2019s uncle.\\n\\nWithin, in the servants\u2019 quarters of the house, the partly dressed domestics spoke together in hushed whispers. Old Mrs. Leaf wept and twisted her hands. Francis was pale as death.\\n\\nAfter some fifteen minutes, he fetched the coachman and one of the footmen, and crept upstairs.\"}"
