          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2fc9bbe6f868bdc99f236069\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cSo I own some knights,\u201d I said as we rode away. \u201cWho would have thought I\u2019d live to count assets like that? I won\u2019t know what to do with them, unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, if it please you, sir, and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a good catch. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I did not understand thee. That I will tell thee soon.\u201d Then she said thoughtfully and softly, tasting the words on her tongue: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; ah, yes; where do they hang out. Truly, the phrase has a sweet and charming grace, and is prettily spoken besides. I will repeat it again and again in my idle hours, so that perhaps I may learn it. Where do they hang out. Just so! Already it trips easily from my tongue, and since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them a little while ago. Figuratively speaking, the game\u2019s called.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Get to bat. I mean, get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t use so much kindling to start your fire. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, and gladly begin. So the two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I saw my mistake at once. I had started her machinery; it was my own fault. She would take thirty days to get down to those facts. She usually began without an introduction and ended without a conclusion. If you interrupted her, she either kept going without noticing, or answered in a few words and then went back and repeated the sentence. So interruptions only made things worse; yet I had to interrupt, and quite often, to save my life. A person would die if he let her monotony drip over him all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said in my misery. She went straight back and began again:\\n\\n\u201cSo the two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, where they were well lodged. In the morning they heard mass in the abbey, then rode on until they came to a great forest. There Sir Gawaine saw, in a valley near a tower, twelve fair damsels and two knights armed upon great horses, and the damsels walked back and forth beside a tree.\u201d\"}"
