          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7e9dea8f1888fc5a1e0d04c8\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so striking in the growing intensity of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s stare, and he seemed to be weighing so many thoughts and becoming so bewildered, that I could not understand him. I thought about it long after he had risen into the clouds inside a large watch-case, and still could not understand it. I was still considering it when I left the theatre an hour later and found him waiting near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I said, shaking his hand as we turned into the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cYes, naturally I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, slipping back into his distracted expression, \u201cand yet I could swear it was him.\u201d\\n\\nAlarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain what he meant.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I would have noticed him at first if you had not been there,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, continuing in the same absent manner, \u201cI cannot say for certain; but I think I would have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around, as I was used to doing when I went home, for his mysterious words sent a chill through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He cannot be in sight,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I came off. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nSince I had reason to be suspicious, I even suspected this poor actor. I feared he was trying to trap me into admitting something. So I looked at him as we walked, but said nothing.\\n\\n\u201cI had the absurd idea that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw that you were entirely unaware of him, sitting behind you like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThat earlier chill came over me again, but I was determined not to speak yet, since his words were entirely consistent with his having been sent to make me connect these hints with Provis. Naturally, I was completely certain that Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say you are wondering about me, Mr. Pip; indeed, I can see that you are. But it is so very strange! You will scarcely believe what I am about to tell you. I could scarcely believe it myself, if you were telling me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cReally?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cNo, truly. Mr. Pip, do you remember, long ago, a certain Christmas Day, when you were a small child and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and some soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it very well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd do you remember that there was a pursuit after two convicts, that we joined it, that Gargery carried you on his back, that I led the way, and that you kept up with me as best you could?\u201d\"}"
