ge himself upon, those who had helped bring about his father\u2019s abdication. In this she failed. Yet the accounts given to him, however distorted, of a great and wise nation claiming its right to govern itself stirred his admiration: from an early age, he became a republican by conviction. Still, his mother did not lose hope. To a love of authority and the proud consciousness of high birth, she added resolute ambition, patience, and self-command. She devoted herself to studying her son\u2019s character. Through praise, rebuke, and persuasion, she sought to find and strike the proper chords; and though the music produced by her touch sounded like discord to her, she placed her hopes in his abilities and remained certain that she would eventually win him over.\"}"
