          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"715fa64465698ae134b857ea\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I was sorry to hear Jim say that; it lowered him so much. My conscience began troubling me worse than ever, until finally I said to it, \u201cLeave me alone\u2014it ain\u2019t too late yet\u2014I\u2019ll paddle ashore at first light and tell.\u201d Right away I felt calm and happy and light as a feather. All my troubles were gone. I started watching closely for a light, and sort of singing to myself. After a while one appeared. Jim called out:\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019s safe, Huck, we\u2019s safe! Jump up and kick yo\u2019 heels! Dat\u2019s good old Cairo at last, I just knows it!\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll take the canoe and go see, Jim. It might not be, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHe jumped up and got the canoe ready, put his old coat in the bottom for me to sit on, and handed me the paddle. As I pushed off, he said:\\n\\n\u201cPooty soon I\u2019ll be shoutin\u2019 for joy, en I\u2019ll say it\u2019s all because of Huck; I\u2019s a free man, en I couldn\u2019t ever ben free if it hadn\u2019 ben for Huck; Huck done it. Jim won\u2019t ever forget you, Huck; you\u2019s de best friend Jim\u2019s ever had; en you\u2019s de only friend old Jim\u2019s got now.\u201d\\n\\nI was paddling away, all worked up to turn him in; but when he said that, it seemed to take all the strength out of me. I went along slowly then, and wasn\u2019t quite sure whether I was glad I had started or not. When I was fifty yards away, Jim said:\\n\\n\u201cDah you goes, de old true Huck; de only white gentleman that ever kept his promise to old Jim.\u201d\\n\\nWell, I felt sick. But I said, I\u2019ve got to do it\u2014I can\u2019t get out of it. Just then a skiff came along with two men in it carrying guns. They stopped, and I stopped. One of them said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that over there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA piece of a raft,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cDo you belong on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAny men on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly one, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, five niggers ran off tonight up yonder, above the head of the bend. Is your man white or black?\u201d\\n\\nI didn\u2019t answer right away. I tried to, but the words would not come. For a second or two I tried to make myself say it, but I wasn\u2019t man enough\u2014I didn\u2019t have the courage of a rabbit. I saw I was giving in, so I stopped trying and said:\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s white.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI reckon we\u2019ll go see for ourselves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI wish you would,\u201d I said, \u201cbecause it\u2019s pap there, and maybe you\u2019d help me tow the raft ashore where the light is.\u201d\"}"
