          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8bc1820b0cfa6efb3a3542f6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u2018If, on the other hand, you require one for domestic use, I can provide you with an excellent specimen, and promise you will be satisfied with the outcome. May I inquire for whom it is meant? If it is for the police, or anybody associated with Scotland Yard, I fear I can be of no assistance. The English detectives are, in truth, our best friends, and I have always discovered that, by trusting to their stupidity, we may do precisely as we please. I could not part with one of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I assure you,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, \u2018it has no connection whatever with the police. Indeed, the clock is meant for the Dean of Chichester.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear me! I had not supposed you held such strong religious feelings, Lord Arthur. Few young men do so nowadays.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I fear you give me too much credit, Herr Winckelkopf,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, colouring. \u2018The truth is, I know absolutely nothing of theology.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Then it is an entirely private affair?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Entirely private.\u2019\\n\\nHerr Winckelkopf shrugged, left the room, and returned a few minutes later carrying a round dynamite cake, about the size of a penny, together with a charming little French clock, topped by an ormolu figure of Liberty crushing the hydra of Despotism beneath her feet.\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s expression lit up at the sight. \u2018That is exactly what I need,\u2019 he exclaimed, \u2018and now tell me how it is set off.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ah! that is my secret,\u2019 replied Herr Winckelkopf, gazing at his invention with a well-earned air of pride; \u2018tell me when you want it to explode, and I shall set the mechanism for that instant.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, this is Tuesday, and if you could dispatch it immediately\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018That cannot be done; I have much important work in hand for certain friends in Moscow. Yet I might send it out to-morrow.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, that will be quite soon enough!\u2019 said Lord Arthur courteously, \u2018provided it is delivered to-morrow evening or on Thursday morning. As for the time of the explosion, let it be Friday at precisely noon. The Dean is invariably at home then.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Friday, at noon,\u2019 repeated Herr Winckelkopf, making a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau beside the fireplace.\\n\\n\u2018And now,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, getting to his feet, \u2018please tell me what I owe you.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018It is so trifling a matter, Lord Arthur, that I have no wish to charge you. The dynamite costs seven and sixpence, the clock three pounds ten, and the carriage perhaps five shillings. I am more than happy to oblige any friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018But your inconvenience, Herr Winckelkopf?\u2019\"}"
