          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7ef4e6f5726d881f8880e379\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away, and immediately set off. When they had gone several miles below \u201cCave Hollow,\u201d Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, you see this bluff looks just alike all the way down from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood-yards, and bushes all alike. But do you see that white spot up yonder where there\u2019s been a landslip? Well, that\u2019s one of my signs. We\u2019ll go ashore now.\u201d\\n\\nThey landed.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, from where we\u2019re standing you could reach that hole I came out of with a fishing-pole. See if you can find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck hunted around the whole place, but found nothing. Tom marched proudly into a dense clump of sumach bushes and said:\\n\\n\u201cHere it is! Look at it, Huck; it\u2019s the coziest hole in this country. You just keep quiet about it. I\u2019ve been wanting all along to be a robber, but I knew I had to have a place like this, and the trouble was where to find one. We\u2019ve got it now, and we\u2019ll keep it secret; only we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in\u2014because, of course, there has to be a Gang, or there wouldn\u2019t be any style to it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds grand, don\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, it surely does, Tom. And who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, nearly anybody. Lay for people\u2014that\u2019s mostly how it\u2019s done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not every time. Keep them in the cave till they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them get all they can from their friends; and after you\u2019ve kept them a year, if it hasn\u2019t been raised by then, you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. Only you don\u2019t kill women. You lock up the women, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always pretty and rich, and terribly frightened. You take their watches and such things, but you always take off your hat and speak politely. Nobody is as polite as robbers\u2014you\u2019ll find that in every book. Then the women come to love you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two, they quit crying, and afterward you couldn\u2019t make them leave. If you turned them out, they\u2019d come straight back. It\u2019s that way in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, that\u2019s mighty fine, Tom. I reckon it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some respects, because it\u2019s near home and circuses and things.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was prepared, and the boys went into the hole, with Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, fastened their spliced kite-strings, and went on.\"}"
