          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"548f744e219c6625d826730a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Raymond paced the room in angry strides. I stood prepared to hear and answer his reproaches. Adrian rested against the wall. \u201cThis is utterly absurd,\u201d he exclaimed; \u201cwere you schoolboys, you could scarcely behave with greater unreason.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou cannot comprehend,\u201d said Raymond. \u201cThis is but one portion of a system\u2014a plan of tyranny to which I will never yield. Because I am Protector of England, must I be the sole slave within its empire? My privacy violated, my conduct condemned, my friends affronted? But I will cast off the whole at once.\u2014Be witnesses,\u201d and he tore the star, the badge of office, from his breast and flung it upon the table. \u201cI resign my office, I surrender my power\u2014let whoever chooses assume it!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet him assume it,\u201d cried Adrian, \u201cwho can call himself, or whom the world can call, your superior. No man exists in England with presumption enough. Know yourself, Raymond, and your anger will vanish; your self-satisfaction return. A few months since, whenever we prayed for our country\u2019s prosperity, or for our own, we likewise prayed for the Protector\u2019s life and welfare, as inseparably bound with it. Your time was given to our advantage; your ambition sought our praise. You adorned our towns with buildings, granted us beneficial institutions, and endowed the soil with plentiful fertility. The mighty and unjust shrank before the steps of your judgment-seat, while the poor and oppressed rose, like flowers awakened by morning, beneath the sunshine of your protection.\\n\\n\u201cCan you marvel that we are all dismayed and grieve when this seems altered? But come, this fit of spleen has already passed; resume your duties; your adherents will welcome you, your enemies fall silent, and our love, honour, and duty will again be shown towards you. Govern yourself, Raymond, and the world obeys you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll this might be excellent sense if spoken to another,\u201d Raymond replied gloomily. \u201cLearn the lesson yourself, and you, the foremost peer of the realm, may become its sovereign. You\u2014the good, wise, and just\u2014may govern every heart. But I see, too early for my own happiness and too late for England\u2019s welfare, that I undertook a charge beyond my strength. I cannot govern myself. My passions rule me; my slightest impulse is my tyrant. Do you suppose I resigned the Protectorate\u2014and I have resigned it\u2014in a moment of spleen? By the living God, I swear I will never take up that trinket again; never again load myself with the burden of care and misery of which it is the outward token.\"}"
