een hearing the arguing voices and forcing open the room door. Some said it was as little as three minutes; others, as much as five. The door was difficult to open.\\n\\n\u201c_Alfonzo Garcio_, an undertaker, states that he lives in the Rue Morgue. He is a native of Spain. He was one of the group who entered the house. He did not go upstairs. He is nervous and feared the effects of excitement. He heard the voices arguing. The rough voice was that of a Frenchman. He could not make out what was said. The high-pitched voice was that of an Englishman\u2014he is certain of it.\"}"
