          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6837920416bc30189d9650ea\",\"rewritten_text\":\"His face was badly sunburned and more than half covered by beard and mustache. He carried a huge oak club, but seemed otherwise unarmed. He bowed awkwardly and wished us \u201cgood evening\u201d in French. His accent was somewhat like that of Neufch\u00e2tel, but still clearly showed that he came from Paris.\\n\\n\u201cSit down, my friend,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cI suppose you have come about the orangutan. Upon my word, I almost envy you for owning him; he is a remarkably fine animal, and no doubt very valuable. How old do you think he is?\u201d\\n\\nThe sailor took a long breath, like a man freed from an unbearable burden, and then answered confidently:\\n\\n\u201cI have no way of knowing\u2014but he cannot be more than four or five years old. Have you got him here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, we have no place to keep him here. He is at a livery stable nearby, in the Rue Dubourg. You can get him in the morning. Of course, you are ready to identify him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly I am, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI shall be sorry to give him up,\u201d said Dupin.\\n\\n\u201cI do not mean for you to take all this trouble for nothing, sir,\u201d said the man. \u201cI would not expect that. I am quite willing to pay a reward for finding the animal\u2014anything reasonable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d replied my friend, \u201cthat is perfectly fair. Let me think\u2014what shall I ask? Ah, I will tell you. My reward will be this: you must give me all the information you can about the murders in the Rue Morgue.\u201d\\n\\nDupin spoke those last words very softly and calmly. Just as calmly, he walked to the door, locked it, and put the key in his pocket. Then he drew a pistol from inside his coat and, without the slightest agitation, laid it on the table.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s face reddened as though he were struggling to breathe. He sprang to his feet and seized his club, but the next moment sank back into his chair, shaking violently, with a face as pale as death. He said nothing. I pitied him deeply.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin kindly, \u201cyou are frightening yourself without cause\u2014you truly are. We mean you no harm at all. I give you my word, as a gentleman and a Frenchman, that we intend no injury to you. I know perfectly well that you are innocent of the horrors in the Rue Morgue. Still, there is no use denying that you are involved in them to some extent.\u201d\"}"
