201cThe will,\u201d Mr. Brownlow continued for him, \u201cwas written in the same spirit as the letter. He spoke of the misery his wife had caused him; of you, his only son, with your defiant nature, vice, malice, and early evil passions, taught to hate him. He left you and your mother an income of eight hundred pounds a year each. He divided the greater part of his property into two equal shares\u2014one for Agnes Fleming, and the other for their child, if it were born alive and lived to come of age.\u201d\"}"
