d as \u2018Black Isaac, or the Huntsman of Hogley Woods,\u2019 he fell badly after stepping on a butter-slide the twins had made from the entrance of the Tapestry Chamber to the top of the oak staircase. This final insult made him so angry that he decided on one last attempt to defend his dignity and social standing. The next night, he would visit the rude young Etonians in his famous role of \u2018Reckless Rupert, or the Headless Earl.\u2019\\n\\nHe had not appeared in this costume for more than seventy years. Indeed, he had not used it since he had frightened the lovely Lady Barbara Modish so badly that she suddenly ended her engagement to the present Lord Canterville\u2019s grandfather and ran away to Gretna Green with handsome Jack Castleton. She declared that nothing in the world could persuade her to marry into a family that allowed such a dreadful ghost to walk up and down the terrace at twilight.\"}"
