          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3558554edd391c60a1bc0a14\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the center of this opening I saw a white spot, though at first I could not tell what it was. I adjusted the telescope\u2019s focus and looked again; then I recognized it as a human skull.\\n\\n\u201cOnce I made that discovery, I was confident the mystery was solved. The words \u2018main branch, seventh limb, east side\u2019 could refer only to the skull\u2019s position in the tree, while \u2018shoot from the left eye of the death\u2019s head\u2019 could have only one meaning in connection with a search for buried treasure. I understood that the plan was to drop a bullet through the skull\u2019s left eye, and that a bee-line\u2014that is, a straight line\u2014drawn from the nearest point of the trunk through \u2018the shot,\u2019 or the place where the bullet landed, and extended fifty feet beyond it, would mark a definite spot. Beneath that spot, I thought, it was at least possible that something valuable had been hidden.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of this,\u201d I said, \u201cis perfectly clear, and though ingenious, still simple and direct. After you left the Bishop\u2019s Hotel, what happened next?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, after carefully noting the tree\u2019s position, I started home. But the moment I left \u2018the devil\u2019s seat,\u2019 the circular opening disappeared, and no matter how I turned, I could not catch sight of it again. What seems to me the greatest cleverness in the whole affair is that, as repeated experiments have convinced me, this circular opening can be seen from no other accessible viewpoint than the narrow ledge on the rock face.\\n\\n\u201cJupiter accompanied me on this trip to the \u2018Bishop\u2019s Hotel.\u2019 He had undoubtedly noticed my distracted manner during the previous weeks and took particular care not to leave me alone. But the next day, rising very early, I managed to slip away from him and went into the hills to look for the tree. After much effort, I found it. When I returned home that night, my valet proposed giving me a whipping. As for the rest of the adventure, I believe you know it as well as I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI assume,\u201d I said, \u201cthat on your first attempt at digging, you missed the spot because of Jupiter\u2019s stupidity in letting the bug fall through the right eye of the skull instead of the left.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly. That mistake shifted \u2018the shot\u2019\u2014that is, the position of the peg nearest the tree\u2014by about two and a half inches. If the treasure had been directly beneath \u2018the shot,\u2019 the error would have mattered little. But \u2018the shot\u2019 and the nearest point of the tree were merely two points used to establish a line of direction. Naturally, however slight the error was at the start, it grew as we followed the line, and by the time we had gone fifty feet, it had led us completely astray.\u201d\"}"
