sure Mr. Wickham\u2019s various creditors in and around Brighton that they will be paid soon, for which I have made myself responsible. Will you also take the trouble of giving similar assurances to his creditors in Meryton? I will add a list of them, based on his information. He has listed all his debts; at least, I hope he has not deceived us. Haggerston has our instructions, and everything will be completed within a week. They will then join his regiment, unless they are first invited to Longbourn; and Mrs. Gardiner tells me that my niece is very eager to see you all before she leaves the south.\u201d\"}"
