to you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll this would be excellent advice if you gave it to someone else,\u201d Raymond replied gloomily. \u201cLearn the lesson yourself, and you, the first peer of the land, may become its sovereign. You\u2014the good, the wise, the just\u2014may rule every heart. But I see, too soon for my own happiness and too late for England\u2019s welfare, that I undertook a task beyond my strength. I cannot govern myself. My passions are my masters; my slightest impulse is my tyrant. Do you think I renounced the Protectorate\u2014and I have renounced it\u2014in a fit of temper? By the living God, I swear I will never take up that trinket again; never again burden myself with the weight of care and misery of which it is the visible sign.\u201d\"}"
