ecome harsh and serious. When Jupiter again tried to muzzle him, the dog resisted furiously, leaped into the hole, and clawed wildly at the earth. Within seconds he uncovered a heap of human bones: two complete skeletons, mixed with several metal buttons and what seemed to be the dust of rotted woolen cloth. A stroke or two of a spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife, and as we dug farther, three or four loose gold and silver coins came to light.\"}"
