 it, as far down as the string will permit\u2014but take care not to release the string.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll dat done, Massa Will; mighty easy ting to put de bug fru de hole\u2014look out for him down dare!\u201d\\n\\nThroughout this conversation, no part of Jupiter\u2019s body was visible; but the beetle, which he had let down, could now be seen at the string\u2019s end, gleaming like a ball of polished gold in the final beams of the setting sun, a few of which still dimly lighted the height on which we stood. The _scarab\u00e6us_ hung wholly free of the branches and, had it been allowed to drop, would have fallen at our feet. Legrand at once seized the scythe and used it to clear a round space, three or four yards across, directly beneath the insect; when this was done, he told Jupiter to release the string and descend from the tree.\"}"
