          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"10738afb2426df0089635164\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you play?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think, sir,\u201d said the spy, in the most humble way, turning to Mr. Lorry, \u201cI may appeal to a gentleman of your age and kindness, and ask you to put it to this other gentleman, so much younger than yourself, whether he can, in any circumstances, reconcile it with his position to play the Ace he has mentioned. I admit that I am a spy, and that it is thought a dishonourable occupation\u2014though someone must do it; but this gentleman is no spy, so why should he lower himself by becoming one?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI play my Ace, Mr. Barsad,\u201d said Carton, answering for himself and looking at his watch, \u201cwithout the slightest hesitation, in a very few minutes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI had hoped, gentlemen,\u201d said the spy, still trying to draw Mr. Lorry into the matter, \u201cthat your respect for my sister\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI could show my respect for your sister in no better way than by finally freeing her from her brother,\u201d said Sydney Carton.\\n\\n\u201cYou do not think so, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have completely made up my mind.\u201d\\n\\nThe spy\u2019s smooth manner, strangely at odds with his showily rough clothes, and probably with his usual behavior, was checked by Carton\u2019s unreadable expression. Carton was a mystery even to men wiser and more honest than Barsad. The spy faltered and lost his way. While he was uncertain, Carton said, returning to his earlier air of studying cards:\\n\\n\u201cAnd now that I think of it, I have a strong feeling that I hold another good card here, one I have not yet named. That friend and fellow-Sheep, who said he had been tending sheep in the country prisons\u2014who was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFrench. You do not know him,\u201d said the spy quickly.\\n\\n\u201cFrench, eh?\u201d Carton repeated thoughtfully, seeming not to notice him, though he repeated his word. \u201cWell, perhaps he is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe is, I assure you,\u201d said the spy. \u201cThough it is not important.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThough it is not important,\u201d Carton repeated in the same automatic tone. \u201cThough it is not important\u2014No, it is not important. No. Still, I know that face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI do not think so. I am sure not. It cannot be,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cIt-can\u2019t-be,\u201d Sydney Carton muttered, thinking back, and idly emptying his glass again\u2014fortunately, it was a small one. \u201cCan\u2019t-be. He spoke good French. Yet he seemed like a foreigner, I thought?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProvincial,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo. Foreign!\u201d cried Carton, striking the table with his open hand as the truth suddenly became clear to him. \u201cCly! Disguised, but the same man. We had that man before us at the Old Bailey.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow you are being hasty, sir,\u201d said Barsad, with a smile that made his hooked nose tilt even farther to one side. \u201cThere, you really give me an advantage over you.\u201d\"}"
