f he is as remarkable as you say, Lady Windermere, I can hardly fail to find him. Describe him to me, and I will bring him to you at once.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, he does not look at all like a cheiromantist. That is, he is neither mysterious nor esoteric nor romantic in appearance. He is a small, stout man, with an odd bald head and large gold-rimmed spectacles; rather midway between a family physician and a country solicitor. I am truly sorry, but it is not my fault. People are so vexing. All my pianists look precisely like poets, and all my poets precisely like pianists; and I recall asking a most terrible conspirator to dinner last season\u2014a man who had blown up ever so many people, who always wore a coat of mail and carried a dagger up his shirt-sleeve\u2014and do you know, when he arrived he looked exactly like a pleasant old clergyman, and spent the whole evening making jokes?\u2019\"}"
